hidden file into the evals folder), /shape-eval and the eval\n    itself may name the evals folder.\n  impact_if_unknown: 'Garura has no build play for an epic yet (that work is business\n    intent #819). If the check names only some plays, a play that builds code but\n    is not on the list can be handed the eval, and a pass then proves less than the\n    intent asks.'\n  user_decision: accepted\n  user_answer: yes — accepted as proposed\n  resolved_at: '2026-10-26T06:52:29Z'\n  resolved_by_run: shape-slice-798-898\n- id: Q-flag-1\n  kind: asked\n  blocking: false"}}}], "from_update": null}
+{"citation_id": "cite-20261026-019", "issue": 798, "play": "shape-slice", "question": "In which order are the features built?", "answer": "fn-795, then fn-818, then fn-798, then fn-898.", "decided_by": "author-slice (via product-os-keeper)", "decided_at": "2026-10-26T07:02:15Z", "trace": [{"asked": "what /shape-plan needs before it runs", "found": "/shape-plan runs after /shape-slice and needs the slice to exist", "source": {"tier": "garura", "path": "product/product-os/software-delivery-planning/cap-718/fn-818/feature.md", "start": 4, "end": 4, "fingerprint": "sha256:994885950cc86d2453e28af308067e90cd83ed82d1ef9626e2a157812c7b8819", "text": "/shape-plan <intent> runs after /shape-slice, on its own. It reads the slice that serves the intent and the ICE of each feature and its capability, once. It writes the intent's one plan file, one epic for the slice, and one story for each feature. It never writes a failure or recovery condition: the slice's hidden file is /shape-slice's (decision 6 of #844). Not built yet (#818).", "version": null, "around": {"start": 1, "end": 7, "text": "# Feature: /shape-plan writes the plan, the epic and the stories\n\n## What it does\n/shape-plan <intent> runs after /shape-slice, on its own. It reads the slice that serves the intent and the ICE of each feature and its capability, once. It writes the intent's one plan file, one epic for the slice, and one story for each feature. It never writes a failure or recovery condition: the slice's hidden file is /shape-slice's (decision 6 of #844). Not built yet (#818).\n\n> To be deepened later: written by /shape-slice for bi-788 at the directional depth. /discover-domains or /discover-capabilities raises it to the detailed depth.\n"}}}, {"asked": "what /shape-eval needs before it runs", "found": "/shape-eval runs after /shape-plan and reads the epic, its stories and the hidden file", "source": {"tier": "garura", "path": "product/product-os/software-delivery-planning/shape-eval/fn-798/feature.md", "start": 4, "end": 4, "fingerprint": "sha256:040588fb1725bd4ef117100580e5eac7418407a4c3f641d07e9f729fa24aa5ac", "text": "/shape-eval <intent> runs after /shape-plan, on its own. It reads the epic, its stories and the slice's hidden file, and writes the eval for the business intent in the plan's evals folder (.garura/project/plans/<plan-id>/evals/<slug>/). No build is given that folder: the build is given the business intent, never the eval (fn-898). Not built yet (#798).", "version": null, "around": {"start": 1, "end": 7, "text": "# Feature: /shape-eval writes the hidden eval\n\n## What it does\n/shape-eval <intent> runs after /shape-plan, on its own. It reads the epic, its stories and the slice's hidden file, and writes the eval for the business intent in the plan's evals folder (.garura/project/plans/<plan-id>/evals/<slug>/). No build is given that folder: the build is given the business intent, never the eval (fn-898). Not built yet (#798).\n\n> To be deepened later: written by /shape-slice for bi-788 at the directional depth. /discover-domains or /discover-capabilities raises it to the detailed depth.\n"}}}, {"asked": "when the checks of #898 are built", "found": "the design orders #898's checks after /shape-eval (step 3 after step 2)", "source": {"tier": "short-term", "path": "798/specs/design.md", "start": 22, "end": 23, "fingerprint": "sha256:f52dce5529cadbb199f4da8c79ecddf7a323312035ac9952c07deb5868d4e36a", "text": "3. #898: a lint check that no build play's inputs name the evals folder, the eval or the hidden file; a check over a build\n   session's ledger that flags a read of the evals folder (it flags, it does not block), with tests.", "version": null, "around": {"start": 19, "end": 26, "text": "2. `/shape-eval` (#798, through `/create-play`): reads the epic, its stories and the hidden file only; writes one eval\n   per slice into `plans/<plan>/evals/<slice>/`, in plain text; each check tests, from the outside through the usage\n   guide, what the business intent promises; anything it cannot test yet is named; one pinned checkpoint.\n3. #898: a lint check that no build play's inputs name the evals folder, the eval or the hidden file; a check over a build\n   session's ledger that flags a read of the evals folder (it flags, it does not block), with tests.\n4. The rules: ADR 049 (\"Encrypting the evals is #828\") and `docs/philosophy/idd-principles.md` (\"the evals are encrypted\")\n   say instead that the build is given the intent, never the eval (through `/record-decision`, amending ADR 049);\n   the ontology and `managing-work.md` match."}}}], "from_update": null}
+{"citation_id": "cite-20261026-020", "issue": 798, "play": "shape-slice", "question": "Which surface does the tester use?", "answer": "the Claude Code command line", "decided_by": "author-slice (via product-os-keeper)", "decided_at": "2026-10-26T07:02:15Z", "trace": [{"asked": "the surface of the kept slice", "found": "the slice record names the Claude Code command line as its surface", "source": {"tier": "garura", "path": "product/product-os/slices/sl-intent-to-design.yaml", "start": 15, "end": 20, "fingerprint": "sha256:4a2bf683f15724c3a5fd145970358fdd638197e1df4e8c2c04441040277a4130", "text": "surface:\n  id: surf-claude-code-cli\n  name: the Claude Code command line\n  persona_ref: product-owner\n  user_action: runs /shape-slice, then /shape-plan, then /shape-eval on a business\n    intent", "version": null, "around": {"start": 12, "end": 20, "text": "  vertical: the Claude Code command line\n  intents:\n  - bi-788\nsurface:\n  id: surf-claude-code-cli\n  name: the Claude Code command line\n  persona_ref: product-owner\n  user_action: runs /shape-slice, then /shape-plan, then /shape-eval on a business\n    intent"}}}, {"asked": "what the outcome asks the product owner to do", "found": "the product owner names a piece of work and agents shape, plan and write its eval", "source": {"tier": "garura", "path": "product/product-os/intents/bi-788.md", "start": 3, "end": 3, "fingerprint": "sha256:2b57e7172fd80751ff52a570a3403dd241d0428ad66919276ada03cc1b2819ab", "text": "**Outcome:** The product owner names a piece of work. Agents shape it into a slice that one person can test, make its plan and write its eval. The product owner confirms each part as it is made.", "version": null, "around": {"start": 1, "end": 6, "text": "# Agents design a named piece of work\n\n**Outcome:** The product owner names a piece of work. Agents shape it into a slice that one person can test, make its plan and write its eval. The product owner confirms each part as it is made.\n\n**Why:** Today the product owner must guide each step of the design by hand. No play designs the work for Garura's own work: the product owner found this while #760 started. When agents do the design, the work is faster and it stays inside its design.\n"}}}], "from_update": null}
+{"citation_id": "cite-20261026-021", "issue": 798, "play": "shape-slice", "question": "Who tests the slice?", "answer": "the product owner (persona product-owner)", "decided_by": "author-slice (via product-os-keeper)", "decided_at": "2026-10-26T07:02:16Z", "trace": [{"asked": "who asked for the intent", "found": "the product owner", "source": {"tier": "garura", "path": "product/product-os/intents/bi-788.md", "start": 7, "end": 7, "fingerprint": "sha256:de0d088eb3f5a54585f8dad0c95013110386f9f7a1d62b20f80df4d6a142a20b", "text": "**Asked by:** the product owner", "version": null, "around": {"start": 4, "end": 10, "text": "\n**Why:** Today the product owner must guide each step of the design by hand. No play designs the work for Garura's own work: the product owner found this while #760 started. When agents do the design, the work is faster and it stays inside its design.\n\n**Asked by:** the product owner\n\n**Proof it is met:**\n- A business intent goes from its issue to an approved design."}}}, {"asked": "the tester of the kept slice", "found": "persona_ref product-owner", "source": {"tier": "garura", "path": "product/product-os/slices/sl-intent-to-design.yaml", "start": 18, "end": 18, "fingerprint": "sha256:3d969030c31daee3dcfff40b9e7df245f6f7fbbfa1285f1acf0886cf77238ddf", "text": "  persona_ref: product-owner", "version": null, "around": {"start": 15, "end": 20, "text": "surface:\n  id: surf-claude-code-cli\n  name: the Claude Code command line\n  persona_ref: product-owner\n  user_action: runs /shape-slice, then /shape-plan, then /shape-eval on a business\n    intent"}}}], "from_update": null}
+{"citation_id": "cite-20261026-022", "issue": 798, "play": "shape-slice", "question": "Which slice serves this business intent, and does it change?", "answer": "The kept slice sl-intent-to-design serves bi-788; it pulls in fn-898 and pushes out nothing.", "decided_by": "author-slice (via product-os-keeper)", "decided_at": "2026-10-26T07:04:07Z", "trace": [{"asked": "the rule that picks the kept slice", "found": "the slice sl-intent-to-design already lists business intent bi-788", "source": {"tier": "short-term", "path": "798/context/shape-slice/serving.json", "start": 2, "end": 3, "fingerprint": "sha256:800e4495dcc64c6accb19ab682d6ef8f14aa8ce92ab8138651f606b2a024444a", "text": "  \"match\": \"sl-intent-to-design\",\n  \"reason\": \"slice 'sl-intent-to-design' already lists business intent 'bi-788'\",", "version": null, "around": {"start": 1, "end": 6, "text": "{\n  \"match\": \"sl-intent-to-design\",\n  \"reason\": \"slice 'sl-intent-to-design' already lists business intent 'bi-788'\",\n  \"reuse_args\": [\n    \"--reuse\",\n    \"sl-intent-to-design\""}}}, {"asked": "the features of the kept slice", "found": "sl-intent-to-design holds fn-795, fn-818 and fn-798, serves bi-788, on the Claude Code command line; it lacks fn-898, which the shaped slice needs", "source": {"tier": "garura", "path": "product/product-os/_spine.yaml", "start": 556, "end": 565, "fingerprint": "sha256:0ea3c68ccb38675e601173f5a27bf2f81f11ad39bf2d12122448c9d9d119e308", "text": "- id: sl-intent-to-design\n  slug: intent-to-design\n  feature_refs:\n  - fn-795\n  - fn-818\n  - fn-798\n  vertical: the Claude Code command line\n  intents:\n  - bi-788\n  record: slices/sl-intent-to-design.yaml", "version": null, "around": {"start": 553, "end": 565, "text": "        no write to Phoenix memory or another project's memory\n  compliance: []\nslices:\n- id: sl-intent-to-design\n  slug: intent-to-design\n  feature_refs:\n  - fn-795\n  - fn-818\n  - fn-798\n  vertical: the Claude Code command line\n  intents:\n  - bi-788\n  record: slices/sl-intent-to-design.yaml"}}}, {"asked": "does fn-795 still serve an intent of the slice", "found": "fn-795 lists bi-788, so it is not pushed out", "source": {"tier": "garura", "path": "product/product-os/_spine.yaml", "start": 454, "end": 455, "fingerprint": "sha256:ded8e679b38b5506d8fb1d8d7440887a076e16254dfda773787e59ea261e6130", "text": "  intents:\n  - bi-788", "version": null, "around": {"start": 451, "end": 458, "text": "- id: fn-795\n  slug: fn-795\n  capability: cap-shape-slice\n  intents:\n  - bi-788\n  status: proposed\n  one_line: From a business intent, /shape-slice writes one slice, its link to the\n    intent and its hidden file, and no plan, epic, story or eval."}}}, {"asked": "does fn-818 still serve an intent of the slice", "found": "fn-818 lists bi-788, so it is not pushed out", "source": {"tier": "garura", "path": "product/product-os/_spine.yaml", "start": 467, "end": 468, "fingerprint": "sha256:ded8e679b38b5506d8fb1d8d7440887a076e16254dfda773787e59ea261e6130", "text": "  intents:\n  - bi-788", "version": null, "around": {"start": 464, "end": 471, "text": "- id: fn-818\n  slug: fn-818\n  capability: cap-718\n  intents:\n  - bi-788\n  status: proposed\n  one_line: From a shaped slice, /shape-plan writes the intent's one plan file, one\n    epic for the slice and one story for each feature."}}}, {"asked": "does fn-798 still serve an intent of the slice", "found": "fn-798 lists bi-788, so it is not pushed out", "source": {"tier": "garura", "path": "product/product-os/_spine.yaml", "start": 480, "end": 481, "fingerprint": "sha256:ded8e679b38b5506d8fb1d8d7440887a076e16254dfda773787e59ea261e6130", "text": "  intents:\n  - bi-788", "version": null, "around": {"start": 477, "end": 484, "text": "- id: fn-798\n  slug: fn-798\n  capability: cap-shape-eval\n  intents:\n  - bi-788\n  status: proposed\n  one_line: From the plan's epic and stories, /shape-eval writes the eval for the\n    business intent in the plan's evals folder, where no builder reads."}}}], "from_update": null}
+{"citation_id": "cite-20261026-023", "issue": 798, "play": "/shape-slice", "question": "Who fixes each Fails if line of fn-798 and fn-898 (the shape-eval capability) when it trips?", "answer": "The builder can fix 10 of the 12 lines alone (mechanical: move the eval, add a check or note, clean the handoff plan, fix the lint or ledger check). F19 and F23 (a builder was given the eval, or a read has no flag) need a person: a builder seeing the test cannot be undone, and only the product owner can say if the build pass still counts.", "decided_by": "product-os-keeper", "decided_at": "2026-10-26T07:06:59Z", "trace": [{"asked": "the handoff rule for who fixes a recovery", "found": "autonomous when recovering is mechanical from what the builder has; human when it needs judgment, an approval, or is irreversible", "source": {"tier": "garura", "path": "core/memory/standards/rules/expectation-generation.md", "start": 49, "end": 61, "fingerprint": "sha256:ae1eaa94de1e792e8810b306f1159eb0ad6907fdbafb3958129ee55ff176233a", "text": "This is the core routing decision, and the seed of `intent-resolver`'s runtime\nrecovery routing and Level 4 autonomous recovery.\n\n- **`autonomous`** when recovering is **mechanical** — a deterministic transform of\n  output the builder already controls: regrouping, rewording, re-staging, re-running,\n  filling a missing field, correcting a format. No new external judgment required.\n- **`human`** when recovering needs **judgment or authority the builder does not\n  hold** — choosing among genuinely ambiguous options, mapping to an external entity\n  (an issue, an owner), granting an approval, or any irreversible / outward-facing\n  decision.\n\n**The test:** \"Can the builder fix this from information it already has,\ndeterministically?\" Yes → `autonomous`. No (needs a human pick, an approval, or a", "version": null, "around": {"start": 46, "end": 64, "text": "\n### The handoff rule (autonomous vs human)\n\nThis is the core routing decision, and the seed of `intent-resolver`'s runtime\nrecovery routing and Level 4 autonomous recovery.\n\n- **`autonomous`** when recovering is **mechanical** — a deterministic transform of\n  output the builder already controls: regrouping, rewording, re-staging, re-running,\n  filling a missing field, correcting a format. No new external judgment required.\n- **`human`** when recovering needs **judgment or authority the builder does not\n  hold** — choosing among genuinely ambiguous options, mapping to an external entity\n  (an issue, an owner), granting an approval, or any irreversible / outward-facing\n  decision.\n\n**The test:** \"Can the builder fix this from information it already has,\ndeterministically?\" Yes → `autonomous`. No (needs a human pick, an approval, or a\nsource of truth it cannot see) → `human`.\n\nWorked example (commit-code): \"a commit mixes concerns\" → autonomous (regroup is"}}}], "from_update": null}
+{"citation_id": "cite-20261026-024", "issue": 798, "play": "shape-slice", "question": "Which features does the slice hold?", "answer": "fn-795, fn-818 and fn-798, kept as they are, and the new feature fn-898 under cap-shape-eval: the build is given the business intent, never the eval; a check flags each build session that read the evals folder, and records the flag in that build run's evidence.", "decided_by": "author-slice (via product-os-keeper)", "decided_at": "2026-10-26T07:10:10Z", "trace": [{"asked": "the features the slice holds now, after the run's last write", "found": "sl-intent-to-design lists fn-795, fn-818, fn-798 and fn-898 and serves bi-788", "source": {"tier": "garura", "path": "product/product-os/_spine.yaml", "start": 569, "end": 579, "fingerprint": "sha256:af180d57e5f35a4f06095e68f002ef5bec89e2cbf5819cc450e9dd1b4bef6808", "text": "- id: sl-intent-to-design\n  slug: intent-to-design\n  feature_refs:\n  - fn-795\n  - fn-818\n  - fn-798\n  - fn-898\n  vertical: the Claude Code command line\n  intents:\n  - bi-788\n  record: slices/sl-intent-to-design.yaml", "version": null, "around": {"start": 566, "end": 579, "text": "        no write to Phoenix memory or another project's memory\n  compliance: []\nslices:\n- id: sl-intent-to-design\n  slug: intent-to-design\n  feature_refs:\n  - fn-795\n  - fn-818\n  - fn-798\n  - fn-898\n  vertical: the Claude Code command line\n  intents:\n  - bi-788\n  record: slices/sl-intent-to-design.yaml"}}}, {"asked": "the new feature's entry and its capability", "found": "fn-898 sits under cap-shape-eval and lists bi-788", "source": {"tier": "garura", "path": "product/product-os/_spine.yaml", "start": 541, "end": 546, "fingerprint": "sha256:01e3aca8d26fc974a3db5f95734698648a5cd013c3b1074a6df73275ddf29c66", "text": "- id: fn-898\n  slug: fn-898\n  capability: cap-shape-eval\n  intents:\n  - bi-788\n  status: proposed", "version": null, "around": {"start": 538, "end": 549, "text": "    the machine, and on each run compare them with Phoenix memory so the project learns\n    when a block changed.\n  doc: software-delivery-planning/initialize/fn-883/feature.md\n- id: fn-898\n  slug: fn-898\n  capability: cap-shape-eval\n  intents:\n  - bi-788\n  status: proposed\n  one_line: A build is given the business intent, never the eval, and a check flags\n    each build session that read the plan's evals folder.\n  doc: software-delivery-planning/shape-eval/fn-898/feature.md"}}}, {"asked": "what the approved design adds to the slice", "found": "add #898's feature, 'the build is given the business intent, never the eval', under the eval capability, into sl-intent-to-design", "source": {"tier": "short-term", "path": "798/specs/design.md", "start": 16, "end": 18, "fingerprint": "sha256:dfde5ebcbe51177a29b7ba060cee9ce4c05de4370cbbb02d41fcba6d6c6229ec", "text": "1. `/shape-slice 788`: add #898's feature (\"the build is given the business intent, never the eval\") under the eval\n   capability, with its ICE, into slice `sl-intent-to-design`, with its hidden-file entry. Its checkpoint needs the\n   product owner's yes. The plan file then marks #898 as that feature's story.", "version": null, "around": {"start": 13, "end": 21, "text": "- The new story #898 (\"Agents build for the business intent, not only to pass the eval\") sits under epic #794. Done.\n\n## Order of work\n1. `/shape-slice 788`: add #898's feature (\"the build is given the business intent, never the eval\") under the eval\n   capability, with its ICE, into slice `sl-intent-to-design`, with its hidden-file entry. Its checkpoint needs the\n   product owner's yes. The plan file then marks #898 as that feature's story.\n2. `/shape-eval` (#798, through `/create-play`): reads the epic, its stories and the hidden file only; writes one eval\n   per slice into `plans/<plan>/evals/<slice>/`, in plain text; each check tests, from the outside through the usage\n   guide, what the business intent promises; anything it cannot test yet is named; one pinned checkpoint."}}}, {"asked": "what story #898 asks the feature to do", "found": "the build is given the intent, never the eval; a check over a build session's ledger flags a read of the evals folder and does not block", "source": {"tier": "short-term", "path": "798/context/shape-slice/feature-issue-898.json", "start": 14, "end": 14, "fingerprint": "sha256:78cb6c5b7711aad46c8b08f69f755396d932dc7e78aee411a6b1004ed3318e91", "text": "  \"stdout\": \"{\\\"body\\\":\\\"Feature: when agents build, they build for the business intent, not only to pass the eval.\\\\n\\\\nThe product owner, 2026-10-26, in the design of #798: \\\\\\\"all of these things, constraints, the setting in the product model, all in plain text. If an agent really wants to go back and read it, it can go back and read everything. The point we're trying to make is that once the slice happens, we need an eval, and that eval is what we need to pass. I just want to make sure that when the agents are building, they don't only think through the evals, but they look at the intent and build for that.\\\\\\\" It replaces #828 (encryption, dropped with reason).\\\\n\\\\n## What it does\\\\n\\\\n- **The build is given the intent, never the eval.** A build's inputs are the slice's stories, each with its scope of work written from the ICE (goals, limits, expectations) and its Context guidance. No build play, build skill or build helper is handed the eval or the hidden file, or their folder. Nothing is hidden: the eval is simply not part of the brief.\\\\n- **A check flags any build that read the evals folder.** Each play run already records its session (the session stamp and its ledger). After a build, a check reads that session's ledger and flags any read of `plans/<plan>/evals/`. It does not block; it makes the shortcut visible.\\\\n- **The eval measures the intent.** The eval play (#798) writes checks that test, from the outside through the usage guide, what the business intent promises, so passing the eval and meeting the intent are the same thing.\\\\n\\\\n## Done when\\\\n\\\\n- No build play's inputs (contracts, context files) name the evals folder, the eval or the hidden file; a lint check fails one that does.\\\\n- A check over a build session's ledger flags a read of the evals folder, with a test that shows it flags one and passes a clean session.\\\\n- The ontology and `managing-work.md` say the build is given the intent, never the eval (not \\\\\\\"the eval is encrypted\\\\\\\").\\\\n\\\\n## Where it sits\\\\n\\\\n- Under epic #794, the epic of slice `sl-intent-to-design`. `/shape-slice` adds its feature to the slice, with its ICE, in the change for #798.\\\\n\\\\n## Not in this story\\\\n\\\\n- Blocking reads by hook (#893, the guardrails).\\\\n- Encryption (#828, dropped).\\\",\\\"closedAt\\\":null,\\\"issueType\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"IT_kwDOFDfBgM41Yree\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"Story\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"A shippable slice of a Feature: one branch, one PR\\\",\\\"color\\\":\\\"YELLOW\\\"},\\\"labels\\\":[],\\\"number\\\":898,\\\"parent\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"I_kwDORA56Ic8AAAABZJxCqw\\\",\\\"number\\\":794,\\\"state\\\":\\\"OPEN\\\",\\\"title\\\":\\\"The shaping loop turns a business intent into a testable slice, its plan and its eval\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://github.com/intent-driven-ai/garura/issues/794\\\"},\\\"state\\\":\\\"OPEN\\\",\\\"subIssues\\\":{\\\"nodes\\\":[],\\\"totalCount\\\":0},\\\"subIssuesSummary\\\":{\\\"completed\\\":0,\\\"percentCompleted\\\":0,\\\"total\\\":0},\\\"title\\\":\\\"Agents build for the business intent, not only to pass the eval: the build is given the intent, never the eval\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://github.com/intent-driven-ai/garura/issues/898\\\"}\\n\",", "version": null, "around": {"start": 11, "end": 17, "text": "      \"number,title,labels,state,body,url,closedAt,issueType,parent,subIssues,subIssuesSummary\"\n    ]\n  ],\n  \"stdout\": \"{\\\"body\\\":\\\"Feature: when agents build, they build for the business intent, not only to pass the eval.\\\\n\\\\nThe product owner, 2026-10-26, in the design of #798: \\\\\\\"all of these things, constraints, the setting in the product model, all in plain text. If an agent really wants to go back and read it, it can go back and read everything. The point we're trying to make is that once the slice happens, we need an eval, and that eval is what we need to pass. I just want to make sure that when the agents are building, they don't only think through the evals, but they look at the intent and build for that.\\\\\\\" It replaces #828 (encryption, dropped with reason).\\\\n\\\\n## What it does\\\\n\\\\n- **The build is given the intent, never the eval.** A build's inputs are the slice's stories, each with its scope of work written from the ICE (goals, limits, expectations) and its Context guidance. No build play, build skill or build helper is handed the eval or the hidden file, or their folder. Nothing is hidden: the eval is simply not part of the brief.\\\\n- **A check flags any build that read the evals folder.** Each play run already records its session (the session stamp and its ledger). After a build, a check reads that session's ledger and flags any read of `plans/<plan>/evals/`. It does not block; it makes the shortcut visible.\\\\n- **The eval measures the intent.** The eval play (#798) writes checks that test, from the outside through the usage guide, what the business intent promises, so passing the eval and meeting the intent are the same thing.\\\\n\\\\n## Done when\\\\n\\\\n- No build play's inputs (contracts, context files) name the evals folder, the eval or the hidden file; a lint check fails one that does.\\\\n- A check over a build session's ledger flags a read of the evals folder, with a test that shows it flags one and passes a clean session.\\\\n- The ontology and `managing-work.md` say the build is given the intent, never the eval (not \\\\\\\"the eval is encrypted\\\\\\\").\\\\n\\\\n## Where it sits\\\\n\\\\n- Under epic #794, the epic of slice `sl-intent-to-design`. `/shape-slice` adds its feature to the slice, with its ICE, in the change for #798.\\\\n\\\\n## Not in this story\\\\n\\\\n- Blocking reads by hook (#893, the guardrails).\\\\n- Encryption (#828, dropped).\\\",\\\"closedAt\\\":null,\\\"issueType\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"IT_kwDOFDfBgM41Yree\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"Story\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"A shippable slice of a Feature: one branch, one PR\\\",\\\"color\\\":\\\"YELLOW\\\"},\\\"labels\\\":[],\\\"number\\\":898,\\\"parent\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"I_kwDORA56Ic8AAAABZJxCqw\\\",\\\"number\\\":794,\\\"state\\\":\\\"OPEN\\\",\\\"title\\\":\\\"The shaping loop turns a business intent into a testable slice, its plan and its eval\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://github.com/intent-driven-ai/garura/issues/794\\\"},\\\"state\\\":\\\"OPEN\\\",\\\"subIssues\\\":{\\\"nodes\\\":[],\\\"totalCount\\\":0},\\\"subIssuesSummary\\\":{\\\"completed\\\":0,\\\"percentCompleted\\\":0,\\\"total\\\":0},\\\"title\\\":\\\"Agents build for the business intent, not only to pass the eval: the build is given the intent, never the eval\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://github.com/intent-driven-ai/garura/issues/898\\\"}\\n\",\n  \"stderr\": \"\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"tree_available\": true"}}}, {"asked": "where the flag is recorded (record entry Q-flag-1, the person's answer)", "found": "the product owner: record the flag under evidence for now; drift checks and evidence warnings come later in Griffin", "source": {"tier": "short-term", "path": "798/context/grounding-questions.md", "start": 34, "end": 53, "fingerprint": "sha256:232f514d96b600531f279de41c3c0e82728df0f70adf2165ba966a9ede8bf149", "text": "- id: Q-flag-1\n  kind: asked\n  blocking: false\n  asked_at: '2026-10-26T06:32:34Z'\n  topic: flag\n  question: Where must the product owner see the flag when a build session read the\n    evals folder?\n  proposed_answer: null\n  basis: null\n  pipeline_source: /shape-slice shape-slice-798-898\n  pipeline_guess: null\n  impact_if_unknown: The check does not block a build; it only makes the read visible.\n    If the flag sits where no person looks, the shortcut stays hidden in practice,\n    and the product owner trusts an eval pass that the builder could aim at.\n  user_decision: in_scope\n  user_answer: this gets recorded in evidence. We will build drift checks and evidence\n    warnings in Griffin so that will be seen there. For now we should record this\n    under evidence.\n  resolved_at: '2026-10-26T06:54:02Z'\n  resolved_by_run: shape-slice-798-898", "version": null, "around": {"start": 31, "end": 56, "text": "  user_answer: yes — accepted as proposed\n  resolved_at: '2026-10-26T06:52:29Z'\n  resolved_by_run: shape-slice-798-898\n- id: Q-flag-1\n  kind: asked\n  blocking: false\n  asked_at: '2026-10-26T06:32:34Z'\n  topic: flag\n  question: Where must the product owner see the flag when a build session read the\n    evals folder?\n  proposed_answer: null\n  basis: null\n  pipeline_source: /shape-slice shape-slice-798-898\n  pipeline_guess: null\n  impact_if_unknown: The check does not block a build; it only makes the read visible.\n    If the flag sits where no person looks, the shortcut stays hidden in practice,\n    and the product owner trusts an eval pass that the builder could aim at.\n  user_decision: in_scope\n  user_answer: this gets recorded in evidence. We will build drift checks and evidence\n    warnings in Griffin so that will be seen there. For now we should record this\n    under evidence.\n  resolved_at: '2026-10-26T06:54:02Z'\n  resolved_by_run: shape-slice-798-898\n- id: Q-proof-1\n  kind: asked\n  blocking: false"}}}, {"asked": "which plays the check treats as build plays (record entry Q-builders-1, the person's answer)", "found": "accepted as proposed: every play, skill and agent that builds the software, and every context sub-agent it starts; only /shape-slice, /shape-eval and the eval may name the evals folder", "source": {"tier": "short-term", "path": "798/context/grounding-questions.md", "start": 7, "end": 33, "fingerprint": "sha256:32c724a66849e3d597cea9aa03e63e5711cc10fe5bd72f11b272667815083977", "text": "- id: Q-builders-1\n  kind: asked\n  blocking: false\n  asked_at: '2026-10-26T06:32:34Z'\n  topic: builders\n  question: Which plays must the new check treat as build plays, whose inputs may\n    never name the evals folder?\n  proposed_answer: Every play, skill and agent that builds the software, and every\n    context sub-agent it starts, is a build play for the check. Only /shape-slice\n    (which writes the hidden file into the evals folder), /shape-eval and the eval\n    itself may name the evals folder.\n  basis:\n    kind: model\n    ref: product/product-os/software-delivery-planning/shape-eval/capability.md:4\n  pipeline_source: /shape-slice shape-slice-798-898\n  pipeline_guess: Every play, skill and agent that builds the software, and every\n    context sub-agent it starts, is a build play for the check. Only /shape-slice\n    (which writes the hidden file into the evals folder), /shape-eval and the eval\n    itself may name the evals folder.\n  impact_if_unknown: 'Garura has no build play for an epic yet (that work is business\n    intent #819). If the check names only some plays, a play that builds code but\n    is not on the list can be handed the eval, and a pass then proves less than the\n    intent asks.'\n  user_decision: accepted\n  user_answer: yes — accepted as proposed\n  resolved_at: '2026-10-26T06:52:29Z'\n  resolved_by_run: shape-slice-798-898", "version": null, "around": {"start": 4, "end": 36, "text": "\n```yaml\nquestions:\n- id: Q-builders-1\n  kind: asked\n  blocking: false\n  asked_at: '2026-10-26T06:32:34Z'\n  topic: builders\n  question: Which plays must the new check treat as build plays, whose inputs may\n    never name the evals folder?\n  proposed_answer: Every play, skill and agent that builds the software, and every\n    context sub-agent it starts, is a build play for the check. Only /shape-slice\n    (which writes the hidden file into the evals folder), /shape-eval and the eval\n    itself may name the evals folder.\n  basis:\n    kind: model\n    ref: product/product-os/software-delivery-planning/shape-eval/capability.md:4\n  pipeline_source: /shape-slice shape-slice-798-898\n  pipeline_guess: Every play, skill and agent that builds the software, and every\n    context sub-agent it starts, is a build play for the check. Only /shape-slice\n    (which writes the hidden file into the evals folder), /shape-eval and the eval\n    itself may name the evals folder.\n  impact_if_unknown: 'Garura has no build play for an epic yet (that work is business\n    intent #819). If the check names only some plays, a play that builds code but\n    is not on the list can be handed the eval, and a pass then proves less than the\n    intent asks.'\n  user_decision: accepted\n  user_answer: yes — accepted as proposed\n  resolved_at: '2026-10-26T06:52:29Z'\n  resolved_by_run: shape-slice-798-898\n- id: Q-flag-1\n  kind: asked\n  blocking: false"}}}], "from_update": null}
+{"citation_id": "cite-20261026-025", "issue": 798, "play": "shape-slice", "question": "In which order are the features built?", "answer": "fn-795, then fn-818, then fn-798, then fn-898.", "decided_by": "author-slice (via product-os-keeper)", "decided_at": "2026-10-26T07:10:10Z", "trace": [{"asked": "what /shape-plan needs before it runs", "found": "/shape-plan runs after /shape-slice and reads the slice that serves the intent", "source": {"tier": "garura", "path": "product/product-os/software-delivery-planning/cap-718/fn-818/feature.md", "start": 4, "end": 4, "fingerprint": "sha256:994885950cc86d2453e28af308067e90cd83ed82d1ef9626e2a157812c7b8819", "text": "/shape-plan <intent> runs after /shape-slice, on its own. It reads the slice that serves the intent and the ICE of each feature and its capability, once. It writes the intent's one plan file, one epic for the slice, and one story for each feature. It never writes a failure or recovery condition: the slice's hidden file is /shape-slice's (decision 6 of #844). Not built yet (#818).", "version": null, "around": {"start": 1, "end": 7, "text": "# Feature: /shape-plan writes the plan, the epic and the stories\n\n## What it does\n/shape-plan <intent> runs after /shape-slice, on its own. It reads the slice that serves the intent and the ICE of each feature and its capability, once. It writes the intent's one plan file, one epic for the slice, and one story for each feature. It never writes a failure or recovery condition: the slice's hidden file is /shape-slice's (decision 6 of #844). Not built yet (#818).\n\n> To be deepened later: written by /shape-slice for bi-788 at the directional depth. /discover-domains or /discover-capabilities raises it to the detailed depth.\n"}}}, {"asked": "what /shape-eval needs before it runs", "found": "/shape-eval runs after /shape-plan and reads the epic, its stories and the slice's hidden file", "source": {"tier": "garura", "path": "product/product-os/software-delivery-planning/shape-eval/fn-798/feature.md", "start": 4, "end": 4, "fingerprint": "sha256:040588fb1725bd4ef117100580e5eac7418407a4c3f641d07e9f729fa24aa5ac", "text": "/shape-eval <intent> runs after /shape-plan, on its own. It reads the epic, its stories and the slice's hidden file, and writes the eval for the business intent in the plan's evals folder (.garura/project/plans/<plan-id>/evals/<slug>/). No build is given that folder: the build is given the business intent, never the eval (fn-898). Not built yet (#798).", "version": null, "around": {"start": 1, "end": 7, "text": "# Feature: /shape-eval writes the hidden eval\n\n## What it does\n/shape-eval <intent> runs after /shape-plan, on its own. It reads the epic, its stories and the slice's hidden file, and writes the eval for the business intent in the plan's evals folder (.garura/project/plans/<plan-id>/evals/<slug>/). No build is given that folder: the build is given the business intent, never the eval (fn-898). Not built yet (#798).\n\n> To be deepened later: written by /shape-slice for bi-788 at the directional depth. /discover-domains or /discover-capabilities raises it to the detailed depth.\n"}}}, {"asked": "when the checks of #898 are built", "found": "the design orders #898's checks (step 3) after /shape-eval (step 2)", "source": {"tier": "short-term", "path": "798/specs/design.md", "start": 22, "end": 23, "fingerprint": "sha256:f52dce5529cadbb199f4da8c79ecddf7a323312035ac9952c07deb5868d4e36a", "text": "3. #898: a lint check that no build play's inputs name the evals folder, the eval or the hidden file; a check over a build\n   session's ledger that flags a read of the evals folder (it flags, it does not block), with tests.", "version": null, "around": {"start": 19, "end": 26, "text": "2. `/shape-eval` (#798, through `/create-play`): reads the epic, its stories and the hidden file only; writes one eval\n   per slice into `plans/<plan>/evals/<slice>/`, in plain text; each check tests, from the outside through the usage\n   guide, what the business intent promises; anything it cannot test yet is named; one pinned checkpoint.\n3. #898: a lint check that no build play's inputs name the evals folder, the eval or the hidden file; a check over a build\n   session's ledger that flags a read of the evals folder (it flags, it does not block), with tests.\n4. The rules: ADR 049 (\"Encrypting the evals is #828\") and `docs/philosophy/idd-principles.md` (\"the evals are encrypted\")\n   say instead that the build is given the intent, never the eval (through `/record-decision`, amending ADR 049);\n   the ontology and `managing-work.md` match."}}}], "from_update": null}
+{"citation_id": "cite-20261026-026", "issue": 798, "play": "shape-slice", "question": "Which surface does the tester use?", "answer": "the Claude Code command line", "decided_by": "author-slice (via product-os-keeper)", "decided_at": "2026-10-26T07:10:10Z", "trace": [{"asked": "the surface of the slice, as written", "found": "surf-claude-code-cli, the Claude Code command line, where the product owner runs /shape-slice, /shape-plan and /shape-eval", "source": {"tier": "garura", "path": "product/product-os/slices/sl-intent-to-design.yaml", "start": 16, "end": 21, "fingerprint": "sha256:4a2bf683f15724c3a5fd145970358fdd638197e1df4e8c2c04441040277a4130", "text": "surface:\n  id: surf-claude-code-cli\n  name: the Claude Code command line\n  persona_ref: product-owner\n  user_action: runs /shape-slice, then /shape-plan, then /shape-eval on a business\n    intent", "version": null, "around": {"start": 13, "end": 21, "text": "  vertical: the Claude Code command line\n  intents:\n  - bi-788\nsurface:\n  id: surf-claude-code-cli\n  name: the Claude Code command line\n  persona_ref: product-owner\n  user_action: runs /shape-slice, then /shape-plan, then /shape-eval on a business\n    intent"}}}, {"asked": "what the intent's outcome asks the product owner to do", "found": "the product owner names a piece of work and confirms each part as agents make it", "source": {"tier": "garura", "path": "product/product-os/intents/bi-788.md", "start": 3, "end": 3, "fingerprint": "sha256:2b57e7172fd80751ff52a570a3403dd241d0428ad66919276ada03cc1b2819ab", "text": "**Outcome:** The product owner names a piece of work. Agents shape it into a slice that one person can test, make its plan and write its eval. The product owner confirms each part as it is made.", "version": null, "around": {"start": 1, "end": 6, "text": "# Agents design a named piece of work\n\n**Outcome:** The product owner names a piece of work. Agents shape it into a slice that one person can test, make its plan and write its eval. The product owner confirms each part as it is made.\n\n**Why:** Today the product owner must guide each step of the design by hand. No play designs the work for Garura's own work: the product owner found this while #760 started. When agents do the design, the work is faster and it stays inside its design.\n"}}}], "from_update": null}
+{"citation_id": "cite-20261026-027", "issue": 798, "play": "shape-slice", "question": "Who tests the slice?", "answer": "the product owner (persona product-owner)", "decided_by": "author-slice (via product-os-keeper)", "decided_at": "2026-10-26T07:10:10Z", "trace": [{"asked": "who asked for the intent", "found": "the product owner", "source": {"tier": "garura", "path": "product/product-os/intents/bi-788.md", "start": 7, "end": 7, "fingerprint": "sha256:de0d088eb3f5a54585f8dad0c95013110386f9f7a1d62b20f80df4d6a142a20b", "text": "**Asked by:** the product owner", "version": null, "around": {"start": 4, "end": 10, "text": "\n**Why:** Today the product owner must guide each step of the design by hand. No play designs the work for Garura's own work: the product owner found this while #760 started. When agents do the design, the work is faster and it stays inside its design.\n\n**Asked by:** the product owner\n\n**Proof it is met:**\n- A business intent goes from its issue to an approved design."}}}, {"asked": "the persona of the slice's surface, as written", "found": "persona_ref product-owner", "source": {"tier": "garura", "path": "product/product-os/slices/sl-intent-to-design.yaml", "start": 19, "end": 19, "fingerprint": "sha256:3d969030c31daee3dcfff40b9e7df245f6f7fbbfa1285f1acf0886cf77238ddf", "text": "  persona_ref: product-owner", "version": null, "around": {"start": 16, "end": 21, "text": "surface:\n  id: surf-claude-code-cli\n  name: the Claude Code command line\n  persona_ref: product-owner\n  user_action: runs /shape-slice, then /shape-plan, then /shape-eval on a business\n    intent"}}}], "from_update": null}
+{"citation_id": "cite-20261026-028", "issue": 798, "play": "shape-slice", "question": "Which slice serves this business intent, and does it change?", "answer": "The kept slice sl-intent-to-design serves bi-788; it pulls in fn-898 and pushes out nothing.", "decided_by": "author-slice (via product-os-keeper)", "decided_at": "2026-10-26T07:10:10Z", "trace": [{"asked": "the rule that picks the kept slice", "found": "the slice sl-intent-to-design already lists business intent bi-788", "source": {"tier": "short-term", "path": "798/context/shape-slice/serving.json", "start": 2, "end": 3, "fingerprint": "sha256:800e4495dcc64c6accb19ab682d6ef8f14aa8ce92ab8138651f606b2a024444a", "text": "  \"match\": \"sl-intent-to-design\",\n  \"reason\": \"slice 'sl-intent-to-design' already lists business intent 'bi-788'\",", "version": null, "around": {"start": 1, "end": 6, "text": "{\n  \"match\": \"sl-intent-to-design\",\n  \"reason\": \"slice 'sl-intent-to-design' already lists business intent 'bi-788'\",\n  \"reuse_args\": [\n    \"--reuse\",\n    \"sl-intent-to-design\""}}}, {"asked": "whether a slice is in progress", "found": "no slice is in progress, so the kept slice may change", "source": {"tier": "short-term", "path": "798/context/shape-slice/serving.json", "start": 8, "end": 8, "fingerprint": "sha256:fbf264c6101df4da7f6b7825b78a7617a59f3586fd7ff9c1c8c19007600f70c5", "text": "  \"in_progress\": []", "version": null, "around": {"start": 5, "end": 9, "text": "    \"--reuse\",\n    \"sl-intent-to-design\"\n  ],\n  \"in_progress\": []\n}"}}}, {"asked": "the slice's spine entry after the run's last write", "found": "sl-intent-to-design serves bi-788 and holds fn-898 as its last feature", "source": {"tier": "garura", "path": "product/product-os/_spine.yaml", "start": 569, "end": 579, "fingerprint": "sha256:af180d57e5f35a4f06095e68f002ef5bec89e2cbf5819cc450e9dd1b4bef6808", "text": "- id: sl-intent-to-design\n  slug: intent-to-design\n  feature_refs:\n  - fn-795\n  - fn-818\n  - fn-798\n  - fn-898\n  vertical: the Claude Code command line\n  intents:\n  - bi-788\n  record: slices/sl-intent-to-design.yaml", "version": null, "around": {"start": 566, "end": 579, "text": "        no write to Phoenix memory or another project's memory\n  compliance: []\nslices:\n- id: sl-intent-to-design\n  slug: intent-to-design\n  feature_refs:\n  - fn-795\n  - fn-818\n  - fn-798\n  - fn-898\n  vertical: the Claude Code command line\n  intents:\n  - bi-788\n  record: slices/sl-intent-to-design.yaml"}}}, {"asked": "does fn-795 still serve bi-788", "found": "fn-795 lists bi-788, so it is not pushed out", "source": {"tier": "garura", "path": "product/product-os/_spine.yaml", "start": 454, "end": 455, "fingerprint": "sha256:ded8e679b38b5506d8fb1d8d7440887a076e16254dfda773787e59ea261e6130", "text": "  intents:\n  - bi-788", "version": null, "around": {"start": 451, "end": 458, "text": "- id: fn-795\n  slug: fn-795\n  capability: cap-shape-slice\n  intents:\n  - bi-788\n  status: proposed\n  one_line: From a business intent, /shape-slice writes one slice, its link to the\n    intent and its hidden file, and no plan, epic, story or eval."}}}, {"asked": "does fn-818 still serve bi-788", "found": "fn-818 lists bi-788, so it is not pushed out", "source": {"tier": "garura", "path": "product/product-os/_spine.yaml", "start": 467, "end": 468, "fingerprint": "sha256:ded8e679b38b5506d8fb1d8d7440887a076e16254dfda773787e59ea261e6130", "text": "  intents:\n  - bi-788", "version": null, "around": {"start": 464, "end": 471, "text": "- id: fn-818\n  slug: fn-818\n  capability: cap-718\n  intents:\n  - bi-788\n  status: proposed\n  one_line: From a shaped slice, /shape-plan writes the intent's one plan file, one\n    epic for the slice and one story for each feature."}}}, {"asked": "does fn-798 still serve bi-788", "found": "fn-798 lists bi-788, so it is not pushed out", "source": {"tier": "garura", "path": "product/product-os/_spine.yaml", "start": 480, "end": 481, "fingerprint": "sha256:ded8e679b38b5506d8fb1d8d7440887a076e16254dfda773787e59ea261e6130", "text": "  intents:\n  - bi-788", "version": null, "around": {"start": 477, "end": 484, "text": "- id: fn-798\n  slug: fn-798\n  capability: cap-shape-eval\n  intents:\n  - bi-788\n  status: proposed\n  one_line: From the plan's epic and stories, /shape-eval writes the eval for the\n    business intent in the plan's evals folder, where no builder reads."}}}, {"asked": "does the pulled-in fn-898 serve bi-788", "found": "fn-898 lists bi-788", "source": {"tier": "garura", "path": "product/product-os/_spine.yaml", "start": 544, "end": 545, "fingerprint": "sha256:ded8e679b38b5506d8fb1d8d7440887a076e16254dfda773787e59ea261e6130", "text": "  intents:\n  - bi-788", "version": null, "around": {"start": 541, "end": 548, "text": "- id: fn-898\n  slug: fn-898\n  capability: cap-shape-eval\n  intents:\n  - bi-788\n  status: proposed\n  one_line: A build is given the business intent, never the eval, and a check flags\n    each build session that read the plan's evals folder."}}}, {"asked": "where the flag is recorded (record entry Q-flag-1, the person's answer)", "found": "the person's change moves where the flag is recorded, under evidence; it adds no feature and removes none", "source": {"tier": "short-term", "path": "798/context/grounding-questions.md", "start": 34, "end": 53, "fingerprint": "sha256:232f514d96b600531f279de41c3c0e82728df0f70adf2165ba966a9ede8bf149", "text": "- id: Q-flag-1\n  kind: asked\n  blocking: false\n  asked_at: '2026-10-26T06:32:34Z'\n  topic: flag\n  question: Where must the product owner see the flag when a build session read the\n    evals folder?\n  proposed_answer: null\n  basis: null\n  pipeline_source: /shape-slice shape-slice-798-898\n  pipeline_guess: null\n  impact_if_unknown: The check does not block a build; it only makes the read visible.\n    If the flag sits where no person looks, the shortcut stays hidden in practice,\n    and the product owner trusts an eval pass that the builder could aim at.\n  user_decision: in_scope\n  user_answer: this gets recorded in evidence. We will build drift checks and evidence\n    warnings in Griffin so that will be seen there. For now we should record this\n    under evidence.\n  resolved_at: '2026-10-26T06:54:02Z'\n  resolved_by_run: shape-slice-798-898", "version": null, "around": {"start": 31, "end": 56, "text": "  user_answer: yes — accepted as proposed\n  resolved_at: '2026-10-26T06:52:29Z'\n  resolved_by_run: shape-slice-798-898\n- id: Q-flag-1\n  kind: asked\n  blocking: false\n  asked_at: '2026-10-26T06:32:34Z'\n  topic: flag\n  question: Where must the product owner see the flag when a build session read the\n    evals folder?\n  proposed_answer: null\n  basis: null\n  pipeline_source: /shape-slice shape-slice-798-898\n  pipeline_guess: null\n  impact_if_unknown: The check does not block a build; it only makes the read visible.\n    If the flag sits where no person looks, the shortcut stays hidden in practice,\n    and the product owner trusts an eval pass that the builder could aim at.\n  user_decision: in_scope\n  user_answer: this gets recorded in evidence. We will build drift checks and evidence\n    warnings in Griffin so that will be seen there. For now we should record this\n    under evidence.\n  resolved_at: '2026-10-26T06:54:02Z'\n  resolved_by_run: shape-slice-798-898\n- id: Q-proof-1\n  kind: asked\n  blocking: false"}}}], "from_update": null}
+{"citation_id": "cite-20261026-029", "issue": 798, "play": "shape-slice", "question": "Which plays must the new check treat as build plays, whose inputs may never name the evals folder? (Q-builders-1)", "answer": "Every play, skill and agent that builds the software, and every context sub-agent it starts, is a build play for the check. Only /shape-slice (which writes the hidden file into the evals folder), /shape-eval and the eval itself may name the evals folder.", "decided_by": "propose-answers (via product-os-keeper)", "decided_at": "2026-10-26T07:10:10Z", "trace": [{"asked": "who may be given the plan's evals folder, on the current line", "found": "no builder, no skill that builds the software and no context sub-agent is given that folder; the build is given the business intent, never the eval, and a check flags each build session that read it and records the flag in that build run's evidence (fn-898)", "source": {"tier": "garura", "path": "product/product-os/software-delivery-planning/shape-eval/capability.md", "start": 4, "end": 4, "fingerprint": "sha256:98f7436574a58e8824f7f4a75ce9294582dd1efea73be549d180dcd8c010caaf", "text": "Write the eval that checks, from the outside, that a business intent is met on its slice's surface. The eval is written before the build, from what the plan wrote: the epic, its stories and the slice's hidden file. It never reads an ICE page itself: each line of an ICE has one reader, /shape-slice for the \"Fails if\" lines and the plan play for the rest (ontology v11, ADR 052). The eval is kept in plain text in the plan's evals folder, and no builder, no skill that builds the software and no context sub-agent is given that folder: the build is given the business intent, never the eval, and a check flags each build session that read the folder and records the flag in that build run's evidence (fn-898). It matters because a builder that sees the test can build to the test, and then a pass proves nothing.", "version": null, "around": {"start": 1, "end": 7, "text": "# Capability: Write the hidden eval\n\n## Directional intent\nWrite the eval that checks, from the outside, that a business intent is met on its slice's surface. The eval is written before the build, from what the plan wrote: the epic, its stories and the slice's hidden file. It never reads an ICE page itself: each line of an ICE has one reader, /shape-slice for the \"Fails if\" lines and the plan play for the rest (ontology v11, ADR 052). The eval is kept in plain text in the plan's evals folder, and no builder, no skill that builds the software and no context sub-agent is given that folder: the build is given the business intent, never the eval, and a check flags each build session that read the folder and records the flag in that build run's evidence (fn-898). It matters because a builder that sees the test can build to the test, and then a pass proves nothing.\n\nFeatures: fn-798 (/shape-eval writes the hidden eval) and fn-898 (the build is given the business intent, never the eval; a check flags each build session that read the evals folder, in that build run's evidence).\n"}}}, {"asked": "which play writes into the evals folder", "found": "/shape-slice writes the slice's hidden file in the plan's evals folder", "source": {"tier": "garura", "path": "product/product-os/software-delivery-planning/shape-slice/fn-795/feature.md", "start": 4, "end": 4, "fingerprint": "sha256:e2ee291f90ccf3c89354da90015cf1f7868c5b1391201868ed80a3eac9446eb7", "text": "/shape-slice <intent> reads the business intent and the product model, asks the person only what the model and memory do not answer, and writes one slice into the spine with its link to the intent. It also writes the slice's hidden file (failure-and-recovery.md, one entry for each feature) in the plan's evals folder, and a thin ICE for each part the slice needs that has no ICE (ontology v11, ADR 052). It writes no plan, no epic, no story and no eval. Built in #795. Not built yet: the hidden file and the thin ICE need the play's /edit-play change (#842).", "version": null, "around": {"start": 1, "end": 7, "text": "# Feature: /shape-slice writes the slice and its hidden file\n\n## What it does\n/shape-slice <intent> reads the business intent and the product model, asks the person only what the model and memory do not answer, and writes one slice into the spine with its link to the intent. It also writes the slice's hidden file (failure-and-recovery.md, one entry for each feature) in the plan's evals folder, and a thin ICE for each part the slice needs that has no ICE (ontology v11, ADR 052). It writes no plan, no epic, no story and no eval. Built in #795. Not built yet: the hidden file and the thin ICE need the play's /edit-play change (#842).\n\n> To be deepened later: written by /shape-slice for bi-788 at the directional depth. /discover-domains or /discover-capabilities raises it to the detailed depth.\n"}}}, {"asked": "did the person accept the proposed answer (record entry Q-builders-1)", "found": "user_decision accepted: 'yes — accepted as proposed'", "source": {"tier": "short-term", "path": "798/context/grounding-questions.md", "start": 7, "end": 33, "fingerprint": "sha256:32c724a66849e3d597cea9aa03e63e5711cc10fe5bd72f11b272667815083977", "text": "- id: Q-builders-1\n  kind: asked\n  blocking: false\n  asked_at: '2026-10-26T06:32:34Z'\n  topic: builders\n  question: Which plays must the new check treat as build plays, whose inputs may\n    never name the evals folder?\n  proposed_answer: Every play, skill and agent that builds the software, and every\n    context sub-agent it starts, is a build play for the check. Only /shape-slice\n    (which writes the hidden file into the evals folder), /shape-eval and the eval\n    itself may name the evals folder.\n  basis:\n    kind: model\n    ref: product/product-os/software-delivery-planning/shape-eval/capability.md:4\n  pipeline_source: /shape-slice shape-slice-798-898\n  pipeline_guess: Every play, skill and agent that builds the software, and every\n    context sub-agent it starts, is a build play for the check. Only /shape-slice\n    (which writes the hidden file into the evals folder), /shape-eval and the eval\n    itself may name the evals folder.\n  impact_if_unknown: 'Garura has no build play for an epic yet (that work is business\n    intent #819). If the check names only some plays, a play that builds code but\n    is not on the list can be handed the eval, and a pass then proves less than the\n    intent asks.'\n  user_decision: accepted\n  user_answer: yes — accepted as proposed\n  resolved_at: '2026-10-26T06:52:29Z'\n  resolved_by_run: shape-slice-798-898", "version": null, "around": {"start": 4, "end": 36, "text": "\n```yaml\nquestions:\n- id: Q-builders-1\n  kind: asked\n  blocking: false\n  asked_at: '2026-10-26T06:32:34Z'\n  topic: builders\n  question: Which plays must the new check treat as build plays, whose inputs may\n    never name the evals folder?\n  proposed_answer: Every play, skill and agent that builds the software, and every\n    context sub-agent it starts, is a build play for the check. Only /shape-slice\n    (which writes the hidden file into the evals folder), /shape-eval and the eval\n    itself may name the evals folder.\n  basis:\n    kind: model\n    ref: product/product-os/software-delivery-planning/shape-eval/capability.md:4\n  pipeline_source: /shape-slice shape-slice-798-898\n  pipeline_guess: Every play, skill and agent that builds the software, and every\n    context sub-agent it starts, is a build play for the check. Only /shape-slice\n    (which writes the hidden file into the evals folder), /shape-eval and the eval\n    itself may name the evals folder.\n  impact_if_unknown: 'Garura has no build play for an epic yet (that work is business\n    intent #819). If the check names only some plays, a play that builds code but\n    is not on the list can be handed the eval, and a pass then proves less than the\n    intent asks.'\n  user_decision: accepted\n  user_answer: yes — accepted as proposed\n  resolved_at: '2026-10-26T06:52:29Z'\n  resolved_by_run: shape-slice-798-898\n- id: Q-flag-1\n  kind: asked\n  blocking: false"}}}], "from_update": null}
+{"citation_id": "cite-20261026-030", "issue": 798, "play": "shape-slice", "question": "Must the proof line of business intent 788 that says no builder can read the eval change to say that no builder is given the eval, with each read flagged? (Q-proof-1)", "answer": "Yes. Change the proof line 'The eval is kept in a place where no builder can read it.' to 'No builder is given the eval, and a check flags each build session that read the evals folder.'", "decided_by": "propose-answers (via product-os-keeper)", "decided_at": "2026-10-26T07:10:10Z", "trace": [{"asked": "does the design still hide the eval from builders", "found": "the product owner dropped encryption: everything is plain text and the goal is not to hide the eval, but that agents build for the intent", "source": {"tier": "short-term", "path": "798/specs/design.md", "start": 7, "end": 10, "fingerprint": "sha256:67276d84990702ee9e707b0af9f4ca80a2d75b31fb402f97e0f517231d9a3f18", "text": "- Encryption is dropped, and #828 with it, closed as not planned with its reason (\"drop encryption and drop 828 ... this\n  feature needs to be dropped with reason. dont reweite 828.\"). Everything (ICE, constraints, the model) is plain text; the\n  goal is not to hide the eval. \"Once the slice happens, we need an eval, and that eval is what we need to pass ... when\n  the agents are building, they don't only think through the evals, but they look at the intent and build for that.\"", "version": null, "around": {"start": 4, "end": 13, "text": "story #898. Running them together saves the pipeline's cost; it says nothing about their plans.\n\n## Decided by the product owner (2026-10-26)\n- Encryption is dropped, and #828 with it, closed as not planned with its reason (\"drop encryption and drop 828 ... this\n  feature needs to be dropped with reason. dont reweite 828.\"). Everything (ICE, constraints, the model) is plain text; the\n  goal is not to hide the eval. \"Once the slice happens, we need an eval, and that eval is what we need to pass ... when\n  the agents are building, they don't only think through the evals, but they look at the intent and build for that.\"\n- Evals stay in the repo (\"you guys can't sit outside\").\n- Rebuilding an eval is wrong: an eval is a fixed yardstick.\n- The new story #898 (\"Agents build for the business intent, not only to pass the eval\") sits under epic #794. Done."}}}, {"asked": "the proof line the answer changes", "found": "the intent page still says the eval is kept in a place where no builder can read it", "source": {"tier": "garura", "path": "product/product-os/intents/bi-788.md", "start": 16, "end": 16, "fingerprint": "sha256:020446553c0733997dd6f6cc8035f143879e6017bccb859b9167f247b3f6452f", "text": "- The eval is kept in a place where no builder can read it.", "version": null, "around": {"start": 13, "end": 19, "text": "- The design has an eval that tests, from the outside, if the business intent is met.\n- Each of the three plays ends at one confirmation by the product owner.\n- A play runs each step. No step is done by hand.\n- The eval is kept in a place where no builder can read it.\n\n**Must not:** Do not send the slice, the plan or the eval to the tracker before the product owner confirms it, and do not start a build before that. Do not let a builder read the eval. Do not shape an ICE that is not ready. Do not ask the person a question that the model or memory answers. Do not include the design, build, test or validation of an epic (#819), the release plays or /learn-outcomes, or the upgrade of an older product model (#835).\n"}}}, {"asked": "did the person accept the proposed answer (record entry Q-proof-1)", "found": "user_decision accepted: 'yes — accepted as proposed'", "source": {"tier": "short-term", "path": "798/context/grounding-questions.md", "start": 54, "end": 78, "fingerprint": "sha256:e24c7e711e34ff64daaf79bfd1408f6d6e259cdadf6a1856f9279f0fadf72e70", "text": "- id: Q-proof-1\n  kind: asked\n  blocking: false\n  asked_at: '2026-10-26T06:32:34Z'\n  topic: proof\n  question: Must the proof line of business intent 788 that says no builder can read\n    the eval change to say that no builder is given the eval, with each read flagged?\n  proposed_answer: Yes. Change the proof line 'The eval is kept in a place where no\n    builder can read it.' to 'No builder is given the eval, and a check flags each\n    build session that read the evals folder.'\n  basis:\n    kind: person\n    ref: 798/specs/design.md:7-10\n  pipeline_source: /shape-slice shape-slice-798-898\n  pipeline_guess: Yes. Change the proof line 'The eval is kept in a place where no\n    builder can read it.' to 'No builder is given the eval, and a check flags each\n    build session that read the evals folder.'\n  impact_if_unknown: 'The product owner dropped encryption: the eval is plain text\n    in the repo, so a builder can open it. The intent page still says no builder can\n    read it. If the words stay, the eval tests a promise the design no longer keeps,\n    and the model and the intent disagree.'\n  user_decision: accepted\n  user_answer: yes — accepted as proposed\n  resolved_at: '2026-10-26T06:52:29Z'\n  resolved_by_run: shape-slice-798-898", "version": null, "around": {"start": 51, "end": 79, "text": "    under evidence.\n  resolved_at: '2026-10-26T06:54:02Z'\n  resolved_by_run: shape-slice-798-898\n- id: Q-proof-1\n  kind: asked\n  blocking: false\n  asked_at: '2026-10-26T06:32:34Z'\n  topic: proof\n  question: Must the proof line of business intent 788 that says no builder can read\n    the eval change to say that no builder is given the eval, with each read flagged?\n  proposed_answer: Yes. Change the proof line 'The eval is kept in a place where no\n    builder can read it.' to 'No builder is given the eval, and a check flags each\n    build session that read the evals folder.'\n  basis:\n    kind: person\n    ref: 798/specs/design.md:7-10\n  pipeline_source: /shape-slice shape-slice-798-898\n  pipeline_guess: Yes. Change the proof line 'The eval is kept in a place where no\n    builder can read it.' to 'No builder is given the eval, and a check flags each\n    build session that read the evals folder.'\n  impact_if_unknown: 'The product owner dropped encryption: the eval is plain text\n    in the repo, so a builder can open it. The intent page still says no builder can\n    read it. If the words stay, the eval tests a promise the design no longer keeps,\n    and the model and the intent disagree.'\n  user_decision: accepted\n  user_answer: yes — accepted as proposed\n  resolved_at: '2026-10-26T06:52:29Z'\n  resolved_by_run: shape-slice-798-898\n```"}}}], "from_update": null}
+{"citation_id": "cite-20261026-031", "issue": 798, "play": "shape-slice", "question": "Which features does the slice hold?", "answer": "fn-795, fn-818 and fn-798, kept as they are, and the new feature fn-898 under cap-shape-eval: the build is given the business intent, never the eval; a check flags each build session that read the evals folder, and records the flag in that build run's evidence.", "decided_by": "author-slice (via product-os-keeper)", "decided_at": "2026-10-26T07:56:18Z", "trace": [{"asked": "the features the slice holds now, after the run's last write", "found": "sl-intent-to-design lists fn-795, fn-818, fn-798 and fn-898 and serves bi-788", "source": {"tier": "garura", "path": "product/product-os/_spine.yaml", "start": 569, "end": 579, "fingerprint": "sha256:af180d57e5f35a4f06095e68f002ef5bec89e2cbf5819cc450e9dd1b4bef6808", "text": "- id: sl-intent-to-design\n  slug: intent-to-design\n  feature_refs:\n  - fn-795\n  - fn-818\n  - fn-798\n  - fn-898\n  vertical: the Claude Code command line\n  intents:\n  - bi-788\n  record: slices/sl-intent-to-design.yaml", "version": null, "around": {"start": 566, "end": 579, "text": "        no write to Phoenix memory or another project's memory\n  compliance: []\nslices:\n- id: sl-intent-to-design\n  slug: intent-to-design\n  feature_refs:\n  - fn-795\n  - fn-818\n  - fn-798\n  - fn-898\n  vertical: the Claude Code command line\n  intents:\n  - bi-788\n  record: slices/sl-intent-to-design.yaml"}}}, {"asked": "the features as the slice record lists them, after the run's repair", "found": "the slice record lists fn-795, fn-818, fn-798 and fn-898", "source": {"tier": "garura", "path": "product/product-os/slices/sl-intent-to-design.yaml", "start": 9, "end": 13, "fingerprint": "sha256:baa3134ed19071bdbd96a14099dbb20338d9b101c65fcc62c1cc017f1212563f", "text": "  feature_refs:\n  - fn-795\n  - fn-818\n  - fn-798\n  - fn-898", "version": null, "around": {"start": 6, "end": 16, "text": "    to test, a plan with one epic and one story for each feature, and an eval that\n    no build is given; a check flags each build session that read the evals folder,\n    and the flag is recorded in that build run's evidence.\n  feature_refs:\n  - fn-795\n  - fn-818\n  - fn-798\n  - fn-898\n  vertical: the Claude Code command line\n  intents:\n  - bi-788"}}}, {"asked": "the new feature's entry and its capability", "found": "fn-898 sits under cap-shape-eval and lists bi-788", "source": {"tier": "garura", "path": "product/product-os/_spine.yaml", "start": 541, "end": 546, "fingerprint": "sha256:01e3aca8d26fc974a3db5f95734698648a5cd013c3b1074a6df73275ddf29c66", "text": "- id: fn-898\n  slug: fn-898\n  capability: cap-shape-eval\n  intents:\n  - bi-788\n  status: proposed", "version": null, "around": {"start": 538, "end": 549, "text": "    the machine, and on each run compare them with Phoenix memory so the project learns\n    when a block changed.\n  doc: software-delivery-planning/initialize/fn-883/feature.md\n- id: fn-898\n  slug: fn-898\n  capability: cap-shape-eval\n  intents:\n  - bi-788\n  status: proposed\n  one_line: A build is given the business intent, never the eval, and a check flags\n    each build session that read the plan's evals folder.\n  doc: software-delivery-planning/shape-eval/fn-898/feature.md"}}}, {"asked": "what the approved design adds to the slice", "found": "add #898's feature, 'the build is given the business intent, never the eval', under the eval capability, into sl-intent-to-design", "source": {"tier": "short-term", "path": "798/specs/design.md", "start": 16, "end": 18, "fingerprint": "sha256:dfde5ebcbe51177a29b7ba060cee9ce4c05de4370cbbb02d41fcba6d6c6229ec", "text": "1. `/shape-slice 788`: add #898's feature (\"the build is given the business intent, never the eval\") under the eval\n   capability, with its ICE, into slice `sl-intent-to-design`, with its hidden-file entry. Its checkpoint needs the\n   product owner's yes. The plan file then marks #898 as that feature's story.", "version": null, "around": {"start": 13, "end": 21, "text": "- The new story #898 (\"Agents build for the business intent, not only to pass the eval\") sits under epic #794. Done.\n\n## Order of work\n1. `/shape-slice 788`: add #898's feature (\"the build is given the business intent, never the eval\") under the eval\n   capability, with its ICE, into slice `sl-intent-to-design`, with its hidden-file entry. Its checkpoint needs the\n   product owner's yes. The plan file then marks #898 as that feature's story.\n2. `/shape-eval` (#798, through `/create-play`): reads the epic, its stories and the hidden file only; writes one eval\n   per slice into `plans/<plan>/evals/<slice>/`, in plain text; each check tests, from the outside through the usage\n   guide, what the business intent promises; anything it cannot test yet is named; one pinned checkpoint."}}}, {"asked": "what story #898 asks the feature to do", "found": "the build is given the intent, never the eval; a check over a build session's ledger flags a read of the evals folder and does not block", "source": {"tier": "short-term", "path": "798/context/shape-slice/feature-issue-898.json", "start": 14, "end": 14, "fingerprint": "sha256:78cb6c5b7711aad46c8b08f69f755396d932dc7e78aee411a6b1004ed3318e91", "text": "  \"stdout\": \"{\\\"body\\\":\\\"Feature: when agents build, they build for the business intent, not only to pass the eval.\\\\n\\\\nThe product owner, 2026-10-26, in the design of #798: \\\\\\\"all of these things, constraints, the setting in the product model, all in plain text. If an agent really wants to go back and read it, it can go back and read everything. The point we're trying to make is that once the slice happens, we need an eval, and that eval is what we need to pass. I just want to make sure that when the agents are building, they don't only think through the evals, but they look at the intent and build for that.\\\\\\\" It replaces #828 (encryption, dropped with reason).\\\\n\\\\n## What it does\\\\n\\\\n- **The build is given the intent, never the eval.** A build's inputs are the slice's stories, each with its scope of work written from the ICE (goals, limits, expectations) and its Context guidance. No build play, build skill or build helper is handed the eval or the hidden file, or their folder. Nothing is hidden: the eval is simply not part of the brief.\\\\n- **A check flags any build that read the evals folder.** Each play run already records its session (the session stamp and its ledger). After a build, a check reads that session's ledger and flags any read of `plans/<plan>/evals/`. It does not block; it makes the shortcut visible.\\\\n- **The eval measures the intent.** The eval play (#798) writes checks that test, from the outside through the usage guide, what the business intent promises, so passing the eval and meeting the intent are the same thing.\\\\n\\\\n## Done when\\\\n\\\\n- No build play's inputs (contracts, context files) name the evals folder, the eval or the hidden file; a lint check fails one that does.\\\\n- A check over a build session's ledger flags a read of the evals folder, with a test that shows it flags one and passes a clean session.\\\\n- The ontology and `managing-work.md` say the build is given the intent, never the eval (not \\\\\\\"the eval is encrypted\\\\\\\").\\\\n\\\\n## Where it sits\\\\n\\\\n- Under epic #794, the epic of slice `sl-intent-to-design`. `/shape-slice` adds its feature to the slice, with its ICE, in the change for #798.\\\\n\\\\n## Not in this story\\\\n\\\\n- Blocking reads by hook (#893, the guardrails).\\\\n- Encryption (#828, dropped).\\\",\\\"closedAt\\\":null,\\\"issueType\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"IT_kwDOFDfBgM41Yree\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"Story\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"A shippable slice of a Feature: one branch, one PR\\\",\\\"color\\\":\\\"YELLOW\\\"},\\\"labels\\\":[],\\\"number\\\":898,\\\"parent\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"I_kwDORA56Ic8AAAABZJxCqw\\\",\\\"number\\\":794,\\\"state\\\":\\\"OPEN\\\",\\\"title\\\":\\\"The shaping loop turns a business intent into a testable slice, its plan and its eval\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://github.com/intent-driven-ai/garura/issues/794\\\"},\\\"state\\\":\\\"OPEN\\\",\\\"subIssues\\\":{\\\"nodes\\\":[],\\\"totalCount\\\":0},\\\"subIssuesSummary\\\":{\\\"completed\\\":0,\\\"percentCompleted\\\":0,\\\"total\\\":0},\\\"title\\\":\\\"Agents build for the business intent, not only to pass the eval: the build is given the intent, never the eval\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://github.com/intent-driven-ai/garura/issues/898\\\"}\\n\",", "version": null, "around": {"start": 11, "end": 17, "text": "      \"number,title,labels,state,body,url,closedAt,issueType,parent,subIssues,subIssuesSummary\"\n    ]\n  ],\n  \"stdout\": \"{\\\"body\\\":\\\"Feature: when agents build, they build for the business intent, not only to pass the eval.\\\\n\\\\nThe product owner, 2026-10-26, in the design of #798: \\\\\\\"all of these things, constraints, the setting in the product model, all in plain text. If an agent really wants to go back and read it, it can go back and read everything. The point we're trying to make is that once the slice happens, we need an eval, and that eval is what we need to pass. I just want to make sure that when the agents are building, they don't only think through the evals, but they look at the intent and build for that.\\\\\\\" It replaces #828 (encryption, dropped with reason).\\\\n\\\\n## What it does\\\\n\\\\n- **The build is given the intent, never the eval.** A build's inputs are the slice's stories, each with its scope of work written from the ICE (goals, limits, expectations) and its Context guidance. No build play, build skill or build helper is handed the eval or the hidden file, or their folder. Nothing is hidden: the eval is simply not part of the brief.\\\\n- **A check flags any build that read the evals folder.** Each play run already records its session (the session stamp and its ledger). After a build, a check reads that session's ledger and flags any read of `plans/<plan>/evals/`. It does not block; it makes the shortcut visible.\\\\n- **The eval measures the intent.** The eval play (#798) writes checks that test, from the outside through the usage guide, what the business intent promises, so passing the eval and meeting the intent are the same thing.\\\\n\\\\n## Done when\\\\n\\\\n- No build play's inputs (contracts, context files) name the evals folder, the eval or the hidden file; a lint check fails one that does.\\\\n- A check over a build session's ledger flags a read of the evals folder, with a test that shows it flags one and passes a clean session.\\\\n- The ontology and `managing-work.md` say the build is given the intent, never the eval (not \\\\\\\"the eval is encrypted\\\\\\\").\\\\n\\\\n## Where it sits\\\\n\\\\n- Under epic #794, the epic of slice `sl-intent-to-design`. `/shape-slice` adds its feature to the slice, with its ICE, in the change for #798.\\\\n\\\\n## Not in this story\\\\n\\\\n- Blocking reads by hook (#893, the guardrails).\\\\n- Encryption (#828, dropped).\\\",\\\"closedAt\\\":null,\\\"issueType\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"IT_kwDOFDfBgM41Yree\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"Story\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"A shippable slice of a Feature: one branch, one PR\\\",\\\"color\\\":\\\"YELLOW\\\"},\\\"labels\\\":[],\\\"number\\\":898,\\\"parent\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"I_kwDORA56Ic8AAAABZJxCqw\\\",\\\"number\\\":794,\\\"state\\\":\\\"OPEN\\\",\\\"title\\\":\\\"The shaping loop turns a business intent into a testable slice, its plan and its eval\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://github.com/intent-driven-ai/garura/issues/794\\\"},\\\"state\\\":\\\"OPEN\\\",\\\"subIssues\\\":{\\\"nodes\\\":[],\\\"totalCount\\\":0},\\\"subIssuesSummary\\\":{\\\"completed\\\":0,\\\"percentCompleted\\\":0,\\\"total\\\":0},\\\"title\\\":\\\"Agents build for the business intent, not only to pass the eval: the build is given the intent, never the eval\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://github.com/intent-driven-ai/garura/issues/898\\\"}\\n\",\n  \"stderr\": \"\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"tree_available\": true"}}}, {"asked": "where the flag is recorded (record entry Q-flag-1, the person's answer)", "found": "the product owner: record the flag under evidence for now; drift checks and evidence warnings come later in Griffin", "source": {"tier": "short-term", "path": "798/context/grounding-questions.md", "start": 34, "end": 53, "fingerprint": "sha256:232f514d96b600531f279de41c3c0e82728df0f70adf2165ba966a9ede8bf149", "text": "- id: Q-flag-1\n  kind: asked\n  blocking: false\n  asked_at: '2026-10-26T06:32:34Z'\n  topic: flag\n  question: Where must the product owner see the flag when a build session read the\n    evals folder?\n  proposed_answer: null\n  basis: null\n  pipeline_source: /shape-slice shape-slice-798-898\n  pipeline_guess: null\n  impact_if_unknown: The check does not block a build; it only makes the read visible.\n    If the flag sits where no person looks, the shortcut stays hidden in practice,\n    and the product owner trusts an eval pass that the builder could aim at.\n  user_decision: in_scope\n  user_answer: this gets recorded in evidence. We will build drift checks and evidence\n    warnings in Griffin so that will be seen there. For now we should record this\n    under evidence.\n  resolved_at: '2026-10-26T06:54:02Z'\n  resolved_by_run: shape-slice-798-898", "version": null, "around": {"start": 31, "end": 56, "text": "  user_answer: yes — accepted as proposed\n  resolved_at: '2026-10-26T06:52:29Z'\n  resolved_by_run: shape-slice-798-898\n- id: Q-flag-1\n  kind: asked\n  blocking: false\n  asked_at: '2026-10-26T06:32:34Z'\n  topic: flag\n  question: Where must the product owner see the flag when a build session read the\n    evals folder?\n  proposed_answer: null\n  basis: null\n  pipeline_source: /shape-slice shape-slice-798-898\n  pipeline_guess: null\n  impact_if_unknown: The check does not block a build; it only makes the read visible.\n    If the flag sits where no person looks, the shortcut stays hidden in practice,\n    and the product owner trusts an eval pass that the builder could aim at.\n  user_decision: in_scope\n  user_answer: this gets recorded in evidence. We will build drift checks and evidence\n    warnings in Griffin so that will be seen there. For now we should record this\n    under evidence.\n  resolved_at: '2026-10-26T06:54:02Z'\n  resolved_by_run: shape-slice-798-898\n- id: Q-proof-1\n  kind: asked\n  blocking: false"}}}, {"asked": "which plays the check treats as build plays (record entry Q-builders-1, the person's answer)", "found": "accepted as proposed: every play, skill and agent that builds the software, and every context sub-agent it starts; only /shape-slice, /shape-eval and the eval may name the evals folder", "source": {"tier": "short-term", "path": "798/context/grounding-questions.md", "start": 7, "end": 33, "fingerprint": "sha256:32c724a66849e3d597cea9aa03e63e5711cc10fe5bd72f11b272667815083977", "text": "- id: Q-builders-1\n  kind: asked\n  blocking: false\n  asked_at: '2026-10-26T06:32:34Z'\n  topic: builders\n  question: Which plays must the new check treat as build plays, whose inputs may\n    never name the evals folder?\n  proposed_answer: Every play, skill and agent that builds the software, and every\n    context sub-agent it starts, is a build play for the check. Only /shape-slice\n    (which writes the hidden file into the evals folder), /shape-eval and the eval\n    itself may name the evals folder.\n  basis:\n    kind: model\n    ref: product/product-os/software-delivery-planning/shape-eval/capability.md:4\n  pipeline_source: /shape-slice shape-slice-798-898\n  pipeline_guess: Every play, skill and agent that builds the software, and every\n    context sub-agent it starts, is a build play for the check. Only /shape-slice\n    (which writes the hidden file into the evals folder), /shape-eval and the eval\n    itself may name the evals folder.\n  impact_if_unknown: 'Garura has no build play for an epic yet (that work is business\n    intent #819). If the check names only some plays, a play that builds code but\n    is not on the list can be handed the eval, and a pass then proves less than the\n    intent asks.'\n  user_decision: accepted\n  user_answer: yes — accepted as proposed\n  resolved_at: '2026-10-26T06:52:29Z'\n  resolved_by_run: shape-slice-798-898", "version": null, "around": {"start": 4, "end": 36, "text": "\n```yaml\nquestions:\n- id: Q-builders-1\n  kind: asked\n  blocking: false\n  asked_at: '2026-10-26T06:32:34Z'\n  topic: builders\n  question: Which plays must the new check treat as build plays, whose inputs may\n    never name the evals folder?\n  proposed_answer: Every play, skill and agent that builds the software, and every\n    context sub-agent it starts, is a build play for the check. Only /shape-slice\n    (which writes the hidden file into the evals folder), /shape-eval and the eval\n    itself may name the evals folder.\n  basis:\n    kind: model\n    ref: product/product-os/software-delivery-planning/shape-eval/capability.md:4\n  pipeline_source: /shape-slice shape-slice-798-898\n  pipeline_guess: Every play, skill and agent that builds the software, and every\n    context sub-agent it starts, is a build play for the check. Only /shape-slice\n    (which writes the hidden file into the evals folder), /shape-eval and the eval\n    itself may name the evals folder.\n  impact_if_unknown: 'Garura has no build play for an epic yet (that work is business\n    intent #819). If the check names only some plays, a play that builds code but\n    is not on the list can be handed the eval, and a pass then proves less than the\n    intent asks.'\n  user_decision: accepted\n  user_answer: yes — accepted as proposed\n  resolved_at: '2026-10-26T06:52:29Z'\n  resolved_by_run: shape-slice-798-898\n- id: Q-flag-1\n  kind: asked\n  blocking: false"}}}], "from_update": null}
+{"citation_id": "cite-20261026-032", "issue": 798, "play": "shape-slice", "question": "In which order are the features built?", "answer": "fn-795, then fn-818, then fn-798, then fn-898.", "decided_by": "author-slice (via product-os-keeper)", "decided_at": "2026-10-26T07:56:18Z", "trace": [{"asked": "what /shape-plan needs before it runs", "found": "/shape-plan runs after /shape-slice and reads the slice that serves the intent", "source": {"tier": "garura", "path": "product/product-os/software-delivery-planning/cap-718/fn-818/feature.md", "start": 4, "end": 4, "fingerprint": "sha256:994885950cc86d2453e28af308067e90cd83ed82d1ef9626e2a157812c7b8819", "text": "/shape-plan <intent> runs after /shape-slice, on its own. It reads the slice that serves the intent and the ICE of each feature and its capability, once. It writes the intent's one plan file, one epic for the slice, and one story for each feature. It never writes a failure or recovery condition: the slice's hidden file is /shape-slice's (decision 6 of #844). Not built yet (#818).", "version": null, "around": {"start": 1, "end": 7, "text": "# Feature: /shape-plan writes the plan, the epic and the stories\n\n## What it does\n/shape-plan <intent> runs after /shape-slice, on its own. It reads the slice that serves the intent and the ICE of each feature and its capability, once. It writes the intent's one plan file, one epic for the slice, and one story for each feature. It never writes a failure or recovery condition: the slice's hidden file is /shape-slice's (decision 6 of #844). Not built yet (#818).\n\n> To be deepened later: written by /shape-slice for bi-788 at the directional depth. /discover-domains or /discover-capabilities raises it to the detailed depth.\n"}}}, {"asked": "what /shape-eval needs before it runs", "found": "/shape-eval runs after /shape-plan and reads the epic, its stories and the slice's hidden file", "source": {"tier": "garura", "path": "product/product-os/software-delivery-planning/shape-eval/fn-798/feature.md", "start": 4, "end": 4, "fingerprint": "sha256:040588fb1725bd4ef117100580e5eac7418407a4c3f641d07e9f729fa24aa5ac", "text": "/shape-eval <intent> runs after /shape-plan, on its own. It reads the epic, its stories and the slice's hidden file, and writes the eval for the business intent in the plan's evals folder (.garura/project/plans/<plan-id>/evals/<slug>/). No build is given that folder: the build is given the business intent, never the eval (fn-898). Not built yet (#798).", "version": null, "around": {"start": 1, "end": 7, "text": "# Feature: /shape-eval writes the hidden eval\n\n## What it does\n/shape-eval <intent> runs after /shape-plan, on its own. It reads the epic, its stories and the slice's hidden file, and writes the eval for the business intent in the plan's evals folder (.garura/project/plans/<plan-id>/evals/<slug>/). No build is given that folder: the build is given the business intent, never the eval (fn-898). Not built yet (#798).\n\n> To be deepened later: written by /shape-slice for bi-788 at the directional depth. /discover-domains or /discover-capabilities raises it to the detailed depth.\n"}}}, {"asked": "when the checks of #898 are built", "found": "the design orders #898's checks (step 3) after /shape-eval (step 2)", "source": {"tier": "short-term", "path": "798/specs/design.md", "start": 22, "end": 23, "fingerprint": "sha256:f52dce5529cadbb199f4da8c79ecddf7a323312035ac9952c07deb5868d4e36a", "text": "3. #898: a lint check that no build play's inputs name the evals folder, the eval or the hidden file; a check over a build\n   session's ledger that flags a read of the evals folder (it flags, it does not block), with tests.", "version": null, "around": {"start": 19, "end": 26, "text": "2. `/shape-eval` (#798, through `/create-play`): reads the epic, its stories and the hidden file only; writes one eval\n   per slice into `plans/<plan>/evals/<slice>/`, in plain text; each check tests, from the outside through the usage\n   guide, what the business intent promises; anything it cannot test yet is named; one pinned checkpoint.\n3. #898: a lint check that no build play's inputs name the evals folder, the eval or the hidden file; a check over a build\n   session's ledger that flags a read of the evals folder (it flags, it does not block), with tests.\n4. The rules: ADR 049 (\"Encrypting the evals is #828\") and `docs/philosophy/idd-principles.md` (\"the evals are encrypted\")\n   say instead that the build is given the intent, never the eval (through `/record-decision`, amending ADR 049);\n   the ontology and `managing-work.md` match."}}}, {"asked": "the order the slice record holds, after the run's repair", "found": "fn-795, fn-818, fn-798, then fn-898", "source": {"tier": "garura", "path": "product/product-os/slices/sl-intent-to-design.yaml", "start": 9, "end": 13, "fingerprint": "sha256:baa3134ed19071bdbd96a14099dbb20338d9b101c65fcc62c1cc017f1212563f", "text": "  feature_refs:\n  - fn-795\n  - fn-818\n  - fn-798\n  - fn-898", "version": null, "around": {"start": 6, "end": 16, "text": "    to test, a plan with one epic and one story for each feature, and an eval that\n    no build is given; a check flags each build session that read the evals folder,\n    and the flag is recorded in that build run's evidence.\n  feature_refs:\n  - fn-795\n  - fn-818\n  - fn-798\n  - fn-898\n  vertical: the Claude Code command line\n  intents:\n  - bi-788"}}}], "from_update": null}
+{"citation_id": "cite-20261026-033", "issue": 798, "play": "shape-slice", "question": "Which surface does the tester use?", "answer": "the Claude Code command line", "decided_by": "author-slice (via product-os-keeper)", "decided_at": "2026-10-26T07:56:18Z", "trace": [{"asked": "the surface of the slice, as the record now holds it", "found": "surf-claude-code-cli, the Claude Code command line", "source": {"tier": "garura", "path": "product/product-os/slices/sl-intent-to-design.yaml", "start": 17, "end": 19, "fingerprint": "sha256:7225003a85ea1a416014bd694206587d61419b97c8bec5a8c4befbbe2be6d2a5", "text": "surface:\n  id: surf-claude-code-cli\n  name: the Claude Code command line", "version": null, "around": {"start": 14, "end": 22, "text": "  vertical: the Claude Code command line\n  intents:\n  - bi-788\nsurface:\n  id: surf-claude-code-cli\n  name: the Claude Code command line\n  persona_ref: product-owner\n  user_action: runs /shape-slice, then /shape-plan, then /shape-eval on a business\n    intent, then runs the check that shows no build play's inputs name the evals folder,"}}}, {"asked": "what the tester does on that surface, as the record now holds it (the text shown in the brief)", "found": "runs /shape-slice, then /shape-plan, then /shape-eval on a business intent, then runs the check that no build play's inputs name the evals folder, and finds the flag of a build session that read it in that build run's evidence", "source": {"tier": "garura", "path": "product/product-os/slices/sl-intent-to-design.yaml", "start": 21, "end": 23, "fingerprint": "sha256:e523119af55037eee500f3c328db74fe964cde2a9b1021a33417b9ff2ef7027f", "text": "  user_action: runs /shape-slice, then /shape-plan, then /shape-eval on a business\n    intent, then runs the check that shows no build play's inputs name the evals folder,\n    and finds the flag of a build session that read it in that build run's evidence", "version": null, "around": {"start": 18, "end": 23, "text": "  id: surf-claude-code-cli\n  name: the Claude Code command line\n  persona_ref: product-owner\n  user_action: runs /shape-slice, then /shape-plan, then /shape-eval on a business\n    intent, then runs the check that shows no build play's inputs name the evals folder,\n    and finds the flag of a build session that read it in that build run's evidence"}}}, {"asked": "the slice's outcome, as the record now holds it (the text shown in the brief)", "found": "the product owner runs three plays and gets a slice, a plan and an eval that no build is given; a check flags each build session that read the evals folder, recorded in that build run's evidence", "source": {"tier": "garura", "path": "product/product-os/slices/sl-intent-to-design.yaml", "start": 5, "end": 8, "fingerprint": "sha256:60d4fb4893b3e251682d00d017e038347a4905eb6f4b9484f38c3a447d71d716", "text": "  outcome: The product owner runs three plays on a business intent and gets a slice\n    to test, a plan with one epic and one story for each feature, and an eval that\n    no build is given; a check flags each build session that read the evals folder,\n    and the flag is recorded in that build run's evidence.", "version": null, "around": {"start": 2, "end": 11, "text": "  id: sl-intent-to-design\n  slug: intent-to-design\n  name: From a named piece of work to its design\n  outcome: The product owner runs three plays on a business intent and gets a slice\n    to test, a plan with one epic and one story for each feature, and an eval that\n    no build is given; a check flags each build session that read the evals folder,\n    and the flag is recorded in that build run's evidence.\n  feature_refs:\n  - fn-795\n  - fn-818"}}}, {"asked": "what the intent's outcome asks the product owner to do", "found": "the product owner names a piece of work and confirms each part as agents make it", "source": {"tier": "garura", "path": "product/product-os/intents/bi-788.md", "start": 3, "end": 3, "fingerprint": "sha256:2b57e7172fd80751ff52a570a3403dd241d0428ad66919276ada03cc1b2819ab", "text": "**Outcome:** The product owner names a piece of work. Agents shape it into a slice that one person can test, make its plan and write its eval. The product owner confirms each part as it is made.", "version": null, "around": {"start": 1, "end": 6, "text": "# Agents design a named piece of work\n\n**Outcome:** The product owner names a piece of work. Agents shape it into a slice that one person can test, make its plan and write its eval. The product owner confirms each part as it is made.\n\n**Why:** Today the product owner must guide each step of the design by hand. No play designs the work for Garura's own work: the product owner found this while #760 started. When agents do the design, the work is faster and it stays inside its design.\n"}}}], "from_update": null}
