s build plays (record entry Q-builders-1, the person's answer)", "found": "accepted as proposed: every play, skill and agent that builds the software, and every context sub-agent it starts; only /shape-slice, /shape-eval and the eval may name the evals folder", "source": {"tier": "short-term", "path": "798/context/grounding-questions.md", "start": 7, "end": 33, "fingerprint": "sha256:32c724a66849e3d597cea9aa03e63e5711cc10fe5bd72f11b272667815083977", "text": "- id: Q-builders-1\n  kind: asked\n  blocking: false\n  asked_at: '2026-10-26T06:32:34Z'\n  topic: builders\n  question: Which plays must the new check treat as build plays, whose inputs may\n    never name the evals folder?\n  proposed_answer: Every play, skill and agent that builds the software, and every\n    context sub-agent it starts, is a build play for the check. Only /shape-slice\n    (which writes the hidden file into the evals folder), /shape-eval and the eval\n    itself may name the evals folder.\n  basis:\n    kind: model\n    ref: product/product-os/software-delivery-planning/shape-eval/capability.md:4\n  pipeline_source: /shape-slice shape-slice-798-898\n  pipeline_guess: Every play, skill and agent that builds the software, and every\n    context sub-agent it starts, is a build play for the check. Only /shape-slice\n    (which writes the hidden file into the evals folder), /shape-eval and the eval\n    itself may name the evals folder.\n  impact_if_unknown: 'Garura has no build play for an epic yet (that work is business\n    intent #819). If the check names only some plays, a play that builds code but\n    is not on the list can be handed the eval, and a pass then proves less than the\n    intent asks.'\n  user_decision: accepted\n  user_answer: yes \u2014 accepted as proposed\n  resolved_at: '2026-10-26T06:52:29Z'\n  resolved_by_run: shape-slice-798-898", "version": null, "around": {"start": 4, "end": 36, "text": "\n```yaml\nquestions:\n- id: Q-builders-1\n  kind: asked\n  blocking: false\n  asked_at: '2026-10-26T06:32:34Z'\n  topic: builders\n  question: Which plays must the new check treat as build plays, whose inputs may\n    never name the evals folder?\n  proposed_answer: Every play, skill and agent that builds the software, and every\n    context sub-agent it starts, is a build play for the check. Only /shape-slice\n    (which writes the hidden file into the evals folder), /shape-eval and the eval\n    itself may name the evals folder.\n  basis:\n    kind: model\n    ref: product/product-os/software-delivery-planning/shape-eval/capability.md:4\n  pipeline_source: /shape-slice shape-slice-798-898\n  pipeline_guess: Every play, skill and agent that builds the software, and every\n    context sub-agent it starts, is a build play for the check. Only /shape-slice\n    (which writes the hidden file into the evals folder), /shape-eval and the eval\n    itself may name the evals folder.\n  impact_if_unknown: 'Garura has no build play for an epic yet (that work is business\n    intent #819). If the check names only some plays, a play that builds code but\n    is not on the list can be handed the eval, and a pass then proves less than the\n    intent asks.'\n  user_decision: accepted\n  user_answer: yes \u2014 accepted as proposed\n  resolved_at: '2026-10-26T06:52:29Z'\n  resolved_by_run: shape-slice-798-898\n- id: Q-flag-1\n  kind: asked\n  blocking: false"}}}], "from_update": null}, {"citation_id": "cite-20261026-019", "issue": 798, "play": "shape-slice", "question": "In which order are the features built?", "answer": "fn-795, then fn-818, then fn-798, then fn-898.", "decided_by": "author-slice (via product-os-keeper)", "decided_at": "2026-10-26T07:02:15Z", "trace": [{"asked": "what /shape-plan needs before it runs", "found": "/shape-plan runs after /shape-slice and needs the slice to exist", "source": {"tier": "garura", "path": "product/product-os/software-delivery-planning/cap-718/fn-818/feature.md", "start": 4, "end": 4, "fingerprint": "sha256:994885950cc86d2453e28af308067e90cd83ed82d1ef9626e2a157812c7b8819", "text": "/shape-plan <intent> runs after /shape-slice, on its own. It reads the slice that serves the intent and the ICE of each feature and its capability, once. It writes the intent's one plan file, one epic for the slice, and one story for each feature. It never writes a failure or recovery condition: the slice's hidden file is /shape-slice's (decision 6 of #844). Not built yet (#818).", "version": null, "around": {"start": 1, "end": 7, "text": "# Feature: /shape-plan writes the plan, the epic and the stories\n\n## What it does\n/shape-plan <intent> runs after /shape-slice, on its own. It reads the slice that serves the intent and the ICE of each feature and its capability, once. It writes the intent's one plan file, one epic for the slice, and one story for each feature. It never writes a failure or recovery condition: the slice's hidden file is /shape-slice's (decision 6 of #844). Not built yet (#818).\n\n> To be deepened later: written by /shape-slice for bi-788 at the directional depth. /discover-domains or /discover-capabilities raises it to the detailed depth.\n"}}}, {"asked": "what /shape-eval needs before it runs", "found": "/shape-eval runs after /shape-plan and reads the epic, its stories and the hidden file", "source": {"tier": "garura", "path": "product/product-os/software-delivery-planning/shape-eval/fn-798/feature.md", "start": 4, "end": 4, "fingerprint": "sha256:040588fb1725bd4ef117100580e5eac7418407a4c3f641d07e9f729fa24aa5ac", "text": "/shape-eval <intent> runs after /shape-plan, on its own. It reads the epic, its stories and the slice's hidden file, and writes the eval for the business intent in the plan's evals folder (.garura/project/plans/<plan-id>/evals/<slug>/). No build is given that folder: the build is given the business intent, never the eval (fn-898). Not built yet (#798).", "version": null, "around": {"start": 1, "end": 7, "text": "# Feature: /shape-eval writes the hidden eval\n\n## What it does\n/shape-eval <intent> runs after /shape-plan, on its own. It reads the epic, its stories and the slice's hidden file, and writes the eval for the business intent in the plan's evals folder (.garura/project/plans/<plan-id>/evals/<slug>/). No build is given that folder: the build is given the business intent, never the eval (fn-898). Not built yet (#798).\n\n> To be deepened later: written by /shape-slice for bi-788 at the directional depth. /discover-domains or /discover-capabilities raises it to the detailed depth.\n"}}}, {"asked": "when the checks of #898 are built", "found": "the design orders #898's checks after /shape-eval (step 3 after step 2)", "source": {"tier": "short-term", "path": "798/specs/design.md", "start": 22, "end": 23, "fingerprint": "sha256:f52dce5529cadbb199f4da8c79ecddf7a323312035ac9952c07deb5868d4e36a", "text": "3. #898: a lint check that no build play's inputs name the evals folder, the eval or the hidden file; a check over a build\n   session's ledger that flags a read of the evals folder (it flags, it does not block), with tests.", "version": null, "around": {"start": 19, "end": 26, "text": "2. `/shape-eval` (#798, through `/create-play`): reads the epic, its stories and the hidden file only; writes one eval\n   per slice into `plans/<plan>/evals/<slice>/`, in plain text; each check tests, from the outside through the usage\n   guide, what the business intent promises; anything it cannot test yet is named; one pinned checkpoint.\n3. #898: a lint check that no build play's inputs name the evals folder, the eval or the hidden file; a check over a build\n   session's ledger that flags a read of the evals folder (it flags, it does not block), with tests.\n4. The rules: ADR 049 (\"Encrypting the evals is #828\") and `docs/philosophy/idd-principles.md` (\"the evals are encrypted\")\n   say instead that the build is given the intent, never the eval (through `/record-decision`, amending ADR 049);\n   the ontology and `managing-work.md` match."}}}], "from_update": null}, {"citation_id": "cite-20261026-020", "issue": 798, "play": "shape-slice", "question": "Which surface does the tester use?", "answer": "the Claude Code command line", "decided_by": "author-slice (via product-os-keeper)", "decided_at": "2026-10-26T07:02:15Z", "trace": [{"asked": "the surface of the kept slice", "found": "the slice record names the Claude Code command line as its surface", "source": {"tier": "garura", "path": "product/product-os/slices/sl-intent-to-design.yaml", "start": 15, "end": 20, "fingerprint": "sha256:4a2bf683f15724c3a5fd145970358fdd638197e1df4e8c2c04441040277a4130", "text": "surface:\n  id: surf-claude-code-cli\n  name: the Claude Code command line\n  persona_ref: product-owner\n  user_action: runs /shape-slice, then /shape-plan, then /shape-eval on a business\n    intent", "version": null, "around": {"start": 12, "end": 20, "text": "  vertical: the Claude Code command line\n  intents:\n  - bi-788\nsurface:\n  id: surf-claude-code-cli\n  name: the Claude Code command line\n  persona_ref: product-owner\n  user_action: runs /shape-slice, then /shape-plan, then /shape-eval on a business\n    intent"}}}, {"asked": "what the outcome asks the product owner to do", "found": "the product owner names a piece of work and agents shape, plan and write its eval", "source": {"tier": "garura", "path": "product/product-os/intents/bi-788.md", "start": 3, "end": 3, "fingerprint": "sha256:2b57e7172fd80751ff52a570a3403dd241d0428ad66919276ada03cc1b2819ab", "text": "**Outcome:** The product owner names a piece of work. Agents shape it into a slice that one person can test, make its plan and write its eval. The product owner confirms each part as it is made.", "version": null, "around": {"start": 1, "end": 6, "text": "# Agents design a named piece of work\n\n**Outcome:** The product owner names a piece of work. Agents shape it into a slice that one person can test, make its plan and write its eval. The product owner confirms each part as it is made.\n\n**Why:** Today the product owner must guide each step of the design by hand. No play designs the work for Garura's own work: the product owner found this while #760 started. When agents do the design, the work is faster and it stays inside its design.\n"}}}], "from_update": null}, {"citation_id": "cite-20261026-021", "issue": 798, "play": "shape-slice", "question": "Who tests the slice?", "answer": "the product owner (persona product-owner)", "decided_by": "author-slice (via product-os-keeper)", "decided_at": "2026-10-26T07:02:16Z", "trace": [{"asked": "who asked for the intent", "found": "the product owner", "source": {"tier": "garura", "path": "product/product-os/intents/bi-788.md", "start": 7, "end": 7, "fingerprint": "sha256:de0d088eb3f5a54585f8dad0c95013110386f9f7a1d62b20f80df4d6a142a20b", "text": "**Asked by:** the product owner", "version": null, "around": {"start": 4, "end": 10, "text": "\n**Why:** Today the product owner must guide each step of the design by hand. No play designs the work for Garura's own work: the product owner found this while #760 started. When agents do the design, the work is faster and it stays inside its design.\n\n**Asked by:** the product owner\n\n**Proof it is met:**\n- A business intent goes from its issue to an approved design."}}}, {"asked": "the tester of the kept slice", "found": "persona_ref product-owner", "source": {"tier": "garura", "path": "product/product-os/slices/sl-intent-to-design.yaml", "start": 18, "end": 18, "fingerprint": "sha256:3d969030c31daee3dcfff40b9e7df245f6f7fbbfa1285f1acf0886cf77238ddf", "text": "  persona_ref: product-owner", "version": null, "around": {"start": 15, "end": 20, "text": "surface:\n  id: surf-claude-code-cli\n  name: the Claude Code command line\n  persona_ref: product-owner\n  user_action: runs /shape-slice, then /shape-plan, then /shape-eval on a business\n    intent"}}}], "from_update": null}, {"citation_id": "cite-20261026-022", "issue": 798, "play": "shape-slice", "question": "Which slice serves this business intent, and does it change?", "answer": "The kept slice sl-intent-to-design serves bi-788; it pulls in fn-898 and pushes out nothing.", "decided_by": "author-slice (via product-os-keeper)", "decided_at": "2026-10-26T07:04:07Z", "trace": [{"asked": "the rule that picks the kept slice", "found": "the slice sl-intent-to-design already lists business intent bi-788", "source": {"tier": "short-term", "path": "798/context/shape-slice/serving.json", "start": 2, "end": 3, "fingerprint": "sha256:800e4495dcc64c6accb19ab682d6ef8f14aa8ce92ab8138651f606b2a024444a", "text": "  \"match\": \"sl-intent-to-design\",\n  \"reason\": \"slice 'sl-intent-to-design' already lists business intent 'bi-788'\",", "version": null, "around": {"start": 1, "end": 6, "text": "{\n  \"match\": \"sl-intent-to-design\",\n  \"reason\": \"slice 'sl-intent-to-design' already lists business intent 'bi-788'\",\n  \"reuse_args\": [\n    \"--reuse\",\n    \"sl-intent-to-design\""}}}, {"asked": "the features of the kept slice", "found": "sl-intent-to-design holds fn-795, fn-818 and fn-798, serves bi-788, on the Claude Code command line; it lacks fn-898, which the shaped slice needs", "source": {"tier": "garura", "path": "product/product-os/_spine.yaml", "start": 556, "end": 565, "fingerprint": "sha256:0ea3c68ccb38675e601173f5a27bf2f81f11ad39bf2d12122448c9d9d119e308", "text": "- id: sl-intent-to-design\n  slug: intent-to-design\n  feature_refs:\n  - fn-795\n  - fn-818\n  - fn-798\n  vertical: the Claude Code command line\n  intents:\n  - bi-788\n  record: slices/sl-intent-to-design.yaml", "version": null, "around": {"start": 553, "end": 565, "text": "        no write to Phoenix memory or another project's memory\n  compliance: []\nslices:\n- id: sl-intent-to-design\n  slug: intent-to-design\n  feature_refs:\n  - fn-795\n  - fn-818\n  - fn-798\n  vertical: the Claude Code command line\n  intents:\n  - bi-788\n  record: slices/sl-intent-to-design.yaml"}}}, {"asked": "does fn-795 still serve an intent of the slice", "found": "fn-795 lists bi-788, so it is not pushed out", "source": {"tier": "garura", "path": "product/product-os/_spine.yaml", "start": 454, "end": 455, "fingerprint": "sha256:ded8e679b38b5506d8fb1d8d7440887a076e16254dfda773787e59ea261e6130", "text": "  intents:\n  - bi-788", "version": null, "around": {"start": 451, "end": 458, "text": "- id: fn-795\n  slug: fn-795\n  capability: cap-shape-slice\n  intents:\n  - bi-788\n  status: proposed\n  one_line: From a business intent, /shape-slice writes one slice, its link to the\n    intent and its hidden file, and no plan, epic, story or eval."}}}, {"asked": "does fn-818 still serve an intent of the slice", "found": "fn-818 lists bi-788, so it is not pushed out", "source": {"tier": "garura", "path": "product/product-os/_spine.yaml", "start": 467, "end": 468, "fingerprint": "sha256:ded8e679b38b5506d8fb1d8d7440887a076e16254dfda773787e59ea261e6130", "text": "  intents:\n  - bi-788", "version": null, "around": {"start": 464, "end": 471, "text": "- id: fn-818\n  slug: fn-818\n  capability: cap-718\n  intents:\n  - bi-788\n  status: proposed\n  one_line: From a shaped slice, /shape-plan writes the intent's one plan file, one\n    epic for the slice and one story for each feature."}}}, {"asked": "does fn-798 still serve an intent of the slice", "found": "fn-798 lists bi-788, so it is not pushed out", "source": {"tier": "garura", "path": "product/product-os/_spine.yaml", "start": 480, "end": 481, "fingerprint": "sha256:ded8e679b38b5506d8fb1d8d7440887a076e16254dfda773787e59ea261e6130", "text": "  intents:\n  - bi-788", "version": null, "around": {"start": 477, "end": 484, "text": "- id: fn-798\n  slug: fn-798\n  capability: cap-shape-eval\n  intents:\n  - bi-788\n  status: proposed\n  one_line: From the plan's epic and stories, /shape-eval writes the eval for the\n    business intent in the plan's evals folder, where no builder reads."}}}], "from_update": null}, {"citation_id": "cite-20261026-023", "issue": 798, "play": "/shape-slice", "question": "Who fixes each Fails if line of fn-798 and fn-898 (the shape-eval capability) when it trips?", "answer": "The builder can fix 10 of the 12 lines alone (mechanical: move the eval, add a check or note, clean the handoff plan, fix the lint or ledger check). F19 and F23 (a builder was given the eval, or a read has no flag) need a person: a builder seeing the test cannot be undone, and only the product owner can say if the build pass still counts.", "decided_by": "product-os-keeper", "decided_at": "2026-10-26T07:06:59Z", "trace": [{"asked": "the handoff rule for who fixes a recovery", "found": "autonomous when recovering is mechanical from what the builder has; human when it needs judgment, an approval, or is irreversible", "source": {"tier": "garura", "path": "core/memory/standards/rules/expectation-generation.md", "start": 49, "end": 61, "fingerprint": "sha256:ae1eaa94de1e792e8810b306f1159eb0ad6907fdbafb3958129ee55ff176233a", "text": "This is the core routing decision, and the seed of `intent-resolver`'s runtime\nrecovery routing and Level 4 autonomous recovery.\n\n- **`autonomous`** when recovering is **mechanical** \u2014 a deterministic transform of\n  output the builder already controls: regrouping, rewording, re-staging, re-running,\n  filling a missing field, correcting a format. No new external judgment required.\n- **`human`** when recovering needs **judgment or authority the builder does not\n  hold** \u2014 choosing among genuinely ambiguous options, mapping to an external entity\n  (an issue, an owner), granting an approval, or any irreversible / outward-facing\n  decision.\n\n**The test:** \"Can the builder fix this from information it already has,\ndeterministically?\" Yes \u2192 `autonomous`. No (needs a human pick, an approval, or a", "version": null, "around": {"start": 46, "end": 64, "text": "\n### The handoff rule (autonomous vs human)\n\nThis is the core routing decision, and the seed of `intent-resolver`'s runtime\nrecovery routing and Level 4 autonomous recovery.\n\n- **`autonomous`** when recovering is **mechanical** \u2014 a deterministic transform of\n  output the builder already controls: regrouping, rewording, re-staging, re-running,\n  filling a missing field, correcting a format. No new external judgment required.\n- **`human`** when recovering needs **judgment or authority the builder does not\n  hold** \u2014 choosing among genuinely ambiguous options, mapping to an external entity\n  (an issue, an owner), granting an approval, or any irreversible / outward-facing\n  decision.\n\n**The test:** \"Can the builder fix this from information it already has,\ndeterministically?\" Yes \u2192 `autonomous`. No (needs a human pick, an approval, or a\nsource of truth it cannot see) \u2192 `human`.\n\nWorked example (commit-code): \"a commit mixes concerns\" \u2192 autonomous (regroup is"}}}], "from_update": null}, {"citation_id": "cite-20261026-024", "issue": 798, "play": "shape-slice", "question": "Which features does the slice hold?", "answer": "fn-795, fn-818 and fn-798, kept as they are, and the new feature fn-898 under cap-shape-eval: the build is given the business intent, never the eval; a check flags each build session that read the evals folder, and records the flag in that build run's evidence.", "decided_by": "author-slice (via product-os-keeper)", "decided_at": "2026-10-26T07:10:10Z", "trace": [{"asked": "the features the slice holds now, after the run's last write", "found": "sl-intent-to-design lists fn-795, fn-818, fn-798 and fn-898 and serves bi-788", "source": {"tier": "garura", "path": "product/product-os/_spine.yaml", "start": 569, "end": 579, "fingerprint": "sha256:af180d57e5f35a4f06095e68f002ef5bec89e2cbf5819cc450e9dd1b4bef6808", "text": "- id: sl-intent-to-design\n  slug: intent-to-design\n  feature_refs:\n  - fn-795\n  - fn-818\n  - fn-798\n  - fn-898\n  vertical: the Claude Code command line\n  intents:\n  - bi-788\n  record: slices/sl-intent-to-design.yaml", "version": null, "around": {"start": 566, "end": 579, "text": "        no write to Phoenix memory or another project's memory\n  compliance: []\nslices:\n- id: sl-intent-to-design\n  slug: intent-to-design\n  feature_refs:\n  - fn-795\n  - fn-818\n  - fn-798\n  - fn-898\n  vertical: the Claude Code command line\n  intents:\n  - bi-788\n  record: slices/sl-intent-to-design.yaml"}}}, {"asked": "the new feature's entry and its capability", "found": "fn-898 sits under cap-shape-eval and lists bi-788", "source": {"tier": "garura", "path": "product/product-os/_spine.yaml", "start": 541, "end": 546, "fingerprint": "sha256:01e3aca8d26fc974a3db5f95734698648a5cd013c3b1074a6df73275ddf29c66", "text": "- id: fn-898\n  slug: fn-898\n  capability: cap-shape-eval\n  intents:\n  - bi-788\n  status: proposed", "version": null, "around": {"start": 538, "end": 549, "text": "    the machine, and on each run compare them with Phoenix memory so the project learns\n    when a block changed.\n  doc: software-delivery-planning/initialize/fn-883/feature.md\n- id: fn-898\n  slug: fn-898\n  capability: cap-shape-eval\n  intents:\n  - bi-788\n  status: proposed\n  one_line: A build is given the business intent, never the eval, and a check flags\n    each build session that read the plan's evals folder.\n  doc: software-delivery-planning/shape-eval/fn-898/feature.md"}}}, {"asked": "what the approved design adds to the slice", "found": "add #898's feature, 'the build is given the business intent, never the eval', under the eval capability, into sl-intent-to-design", "source": {"tier": "short-term", "path": "798/specs/design.md", "start": 16, "end": 18, "fingerprint": "sha256:dfde5ebcbe51177a29b7ba060cee9ce4c05de4370cbbb02d41fcba6d6c6229ec", "text": "1. `/shape-slice 788`: add #898's feature (\"the build is given the business intent, never the eval\") under the eval\n   capability, with its ICE, into slice `sl-intent-to-design`, with its hidden-file entry. Its checkpoint needs the\n   product owner's yes. The plan file then marks #898 as that feature's story.", "version": null, "around": {"start": 13, "end": 21, "text": "- The new story #898 (\"Agents build for the business intent, not only to pass the eval\") sits under epic #794. Done.\n\n## Order of work\n1. `/shape-slice 788`: add #898's feature (\"the build is given the business intent, never the eval\") under the eval\n   capability, with its ICE, into slice `sl-intent-to-design`, with its hidden-file entry. Its checkpoint needs the\n   product owner's yes. The plan file then marks #898 as that feature's story.\n2. `/shape-eval` (#798, through `/create-play`): reads the epic, its stories and the hidden file only; writes one eval\n   per slice into `plans/<plan>/evals/<slice>/`, in plain text; each check tests, from the outside through the usage\n   guide, what the business intent promises; anything it cannot test yet is named; one pinned checkpoint."}}}, {"asked": "what story #898 asks the feature to do", "found": "the build is given the intent, never the eval; a check over a build session's ledger flags a read of the evals folder and does not block", "source": {"tier": "short-term", "path": "798/context/shape-slice/feature-issue-898.json", "start": 14, "end": 14, "fingerprint": "sha256:78cb6c5b7711aad46c8b08f69f755396d932dc7e78aee411a6b1004ed3318e91", "text": "  \"stdout\": \"{\\\"body\\\":\\\"Feature: when agents build, they build for the business intent, not only to pass the eval.\\\\n\\\\nThe product owner, 2026-10-26, in the design of #798: \\\\\\\"all of these things, constraints, the setting in the product model, all in plain text. If an agent really wants to go back and read it, it can go back and read everything. The point we're trying to make is that once the slice happens, we need an eval, and that eval is what we need to pass. I just want to make sure that when the agents are building, they don't only think through the evals, but they look at the intent and build for that.\\\\\\\" It replaces #828 (encryption, dropped with reason).\\\\n\\\\n## What it does\\\\n\\\\n- **The build is given the intent, never the eval.** A build's inputs are the slice's stories, each with its scope of work written from the ICE (goals, limits, expectations) and its Context guidance. No build play, build skill or build helper is handed the eval or the hidden file, or their folder. Nothing is hidden: the eval is simply not part of the brief.\\\\n- **A check flags any build that read the evals folder.** Each play run already records its session (the session stamp and its ledger). After a build, a check reads that session's ledger and flags any read of `plans/<plan>/evals/`. It does not block; it makes the shortcut visible.\\\\n- **The eval measures the intent.** The eval play (#798) writes checks that test, from the outside through the usage guide, what the business intent promises, so passing the eval and meeting the intent are the same thing.\\\\n\\\\n## Done when\\\\n\\\\n- No build play's inputs (contracts, context files) name the evals folder, the eval or the hidden file; a lint check fails one that does.\\\\n- A check over a build session's ledger flags a read of the evals folder, with a test that shows it flags one and passes a clean session.\\\\n- The ontology and `managing-work.md` say the build is given the intent, never the eval (not \\\\\\\"the eval is encrypted\\\\\\\").\\\\n\\\\n## Where it sits\\\\n\\\\n- Under epic #794, the epic of slice `sl-intent-to-design`. `/shape-slice` adds its feature to the slice, with its ICE, in the change for #798.\\\\n\\\\n## Not in this story\\\\n\\\\n- Blocking reads by hook (#893, the guardrails).\\\\n- Encryption (#828, dropped).\\\",\\\"closedAt\\\":null,\\\"issueType\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"IT_kwDOFDfBgM41Yree\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"Story\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"A shippable slice of a Feature: one branch, one PR\\\",\\\"color\\\":\\\"YELLOW\\\"},\\\"labels\\\":[],\\\"number\\\":898,\\\"parent\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"I_kwDORA56Ic8AAAABZJxCqw\\\",\\\"number\\\":794,\\\"state\\\":\\\"OPEN\\\",\\\"title\\\":\\\"The shaping loop turns a business intent into a testable slice, its plan and its eval\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://github.com/intent-driven-ai/garura/issues/794\\\"},\\\"state\\\":\\\"OPEN\\\",\\\"subIssues\\\":{\\\"nodes\\\":[],\\\"totalCount\\\":0},\\\"subIssuesSummary\\\":{\\\"completed\\\":0,\\\"percentCompleted\\\":0,\\\"total\\\":0},\\\"title\\\":\\\"Agents build for the business intent, not only to pass the eval: the build is given the intent, never the eval\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://github.com/intent-driven-ai/garura/issues/898\\\"}\\n\",", "version": null, "around": {"start": 11, "end": 17, "text": "      \"number,title,labels,state,body,url,closedAt,issueType,parent,subIssues,subIssuesSummary\"\n    ]\n  ],\n  \"stdout\": \"{\\\"body\\\":\\\"Feature: when agents build, they build for the business intent, not only to pass the eval.\\\\n\\\\nThe product owner, 2026-10-26, in the design of #798: \\\\\\\"all of these things, constraints, the setting in the product model, all in plain text. If an agent really wants to go back and read it, it can go back and read everything. The point we're trying to make is that once the slice happens, we need an eval, and that eval is what we need to pass. I just want to make sure that when the agents are building, they don't only think through the evals, but they look at the intent and build for that.\\\\\\\" It replaces #828 (encryption, dropped with reason).\\\\n\\\\n## What it does\\\\n\\\\n- **The build is given the intent, never the eval.** A build's inputs are the slice's stories, each with its scope of work written from the ICE (goals, limits, expectations) and its Context guidance. No build play, build skill or build helper is handed the eval or the hidden file, or their folder. Nothing is hidden: the eval is simply not part of the brief.\\\\n- **A check flags any build that read the evals folder.** Each play run already records its session (the session stamp and its ledger). After a build, a check reads that session's ledger and flags any read of `plans/<plan>/evals/`. It does not block; it makes the shortcut visible.\\\\n- **The eval measures the intent.** The eval play (#798) writes checks that test, from the outside through the usage guide, what the business intent promises, so passing the eval and meeting the intent are the same thing.\\\\n\\\\n## Done when\\\\n\\\\n- No build play's inputs (contracts, context files) name the evals folder, the eval or the hidden file; a lint check fails one that does.\\\\n- A check over a build session's ledger flags a read of the evals folder, with a test that shows it flags one and passes a clean session.\\\\n- The ontology and `managing-work.md` say the build is given the intent, never the eval (not \\\\\\\"the eval is encrypted\\\\\\\").\\\\n\\\\n## Where it sits\\\\n\\\\n- Under epic #794, the epic of slice `sl-intent-to-design`. `/shape-slice` adds its feature to the slice, with its ICE, in the change for #798.\\\\n\\\\n## Not in this story\\\\n\\\\n- Blocking reads by hook (#893, the guardrails).\\\\n- Encryption (#828, dropped).\\\",\\\"closedAt\\\":null,\\\"issueType\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"IT_kwDOFDfBgM41Yree\\\",\\\"name\\\":\\\"Story\\\",\\\"description\\\":\\\"A shippable slice of a Feature: one branch, one PR\\\",\\\"color\\\":\\\"YELLOW\\\"},\\\"labels\\\":[],\\\"number\\\":898,\\\"parent\\\":{\\\"id\\\":\\\"I_kwDORA56Ic8AAAABZJxCqw\\\",\\\"number\\\":794,\\\"state\\\":\\\"OPEN\\\",\\\"title\\\":\\\"The shaping loop turns a business intent into a testable slice, its plan and its eval\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://github.com/intent-driven-ai/garura/issues/794\\\"},\\\"state\\\":\\\"OPEN\\\",\\\"subIssues\\\":{\\\"nodes\\\":[],\\\"totalCount\\\":0},\\\"subIssuesSummary\\\":{\\\"completed\\\":0,\\\"percentCompleted\\\":0,\\\"total\\\":0},\\\"title\\\":\\\"Agents build for the business intent, not only to pass the eval: the build is given the intent, never the eval\\\",\\\"url\\\":\\\"https://github.com/intent-driven-ai/garura/issues/898\\\"}\\n\",\n  \"stderr\": \"\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"tree_available\": true"}}}, {"asked": "where the flag is recorded (record entry Q-flag-1, the person's answer)", "found": "the product owner: record the flag under evidence for now; drift checks and evidence warnings come later in Griffin", "source": {"tier": "short-term", "path": "798/context/grounding-questions.md", "start": 34, "end": 53, "fingerprint": "sha256:232f514d96b600531f279de41c3c0e82728df0f70adf2165ba966a9ede8bf149", "text": "- id: Q-flag-1\n  kind: asked\n  blocking: false\n  asked_at: '2026-10-26T06:32:34Z'\n  topic: flag\n  question: Where must the product owner see the flag when a build session read the\n    evals folder?\n  proposed_answer: null\n  basis: null\n  pipeline_source: /shape-slice shape-slice-798-898\n  pipeline_guess: null\n  impact_if_unknown: The check does not block a build; it only makes the read visible.\n    If the flag sits where no person looks, the shortcut stays hidden in practice,\n    and the product owner trusts an eval pass that the builder could aim at.\n  user_decision: in_scope\n  user_answer: this gets recorded in evidence. We will build drift checks and evidence\n    warnings in Griffin so that will be seen there. For now we should record this\n    under evidence.\n  resolved_at: '2026-10-26T06:54:02Z'\n  resolved_by_run: shape-slice-798-898", "version": null, "around": {"start": 31, "end": 56, "text": "  user_answer: yes \u2014 accepted as proposed\n  resolved_at: '2026-10-26T06:52:29Z'\n  resolved_by_run: shape-slice-798-898\n- id: Q-flag-1\n  kind: asked\n  blocking: false\n  asked_at: '2026-10-26T06:32:34Z'\n  topic: flag\n  question: Where must the product owner see the flag when a build session read the\n    evals folder?\n  proposed_answer: null\n  basis: null\n  pipeline_source: /shape-slice shape-slice-798-898\n  pipeline_guess: null\n  impact_if_unknown: The check does not block a build; it only makes the read visible.\n    If the flag sits where no person looks, the shortcut stays hidden in practice,\n    and the product owner trusts an eval pass that the builder could aim at.\n  user_decision: in_scope\n  user_answer: this gets recorded in evidence. We will build drift checks and evidence\n    warnings in Griffin so that will be seen there. For now we should record this\n    under evidence.\n  resolved_at: '2026-10-26T06:54:02Z'\n  resolved_by_run: shape-slice-798-898\n- id: Q-proof-1\n  kind: asked\n  blocking: false"}}}, {"asked": "which plays the check treats as build plays (record entry Q-builders-1, the person's answer)", "found": "accepted as proposed: every play, skill and agent that builds the software, and every context sub-agent it starts; only /shape-slice, /shape-eval and the eval may name the evals folder", "source": {"tier": "short-term", "path": "798/context/grounding-questions.md", "start": 7, "end": 33, "fingerprint": "sha256:32c724a66849e3d597cea9aa03e63e5711cc10fe5bd72f11b272667815083977", "text": "- id: Q-builders-1\n  kind: asked\n  blocking: false\n  asked_at: '2026-10-26T06:32:34Z'\n  topic: builders\n  question: Which plays must the new check treat as build plays, whose inputs may\n    never name the evals folder?\n  proposed_answer: Every play, skill and agent that builds the software, and every\n    context sub-agent it starts, is a build play for the check. Only /shape-slice\n    (which writes the hidden file into the evals folder), /shape-eval and the eval\n    itself may name the evals folder.\n  basis:\n    kind: model\n    ref: product/product-os/software-delivery-planning/shape-eval/capability.md:4\n  pipeline_source: /shape-slice shape-slice-798-898\n  pipeline_guess: Every play, skill and agent that builds the software, and every\n    context sub-agent it starts, is a build play for the check. Only /shape-slice\n    (which writes the hidden file into the evals folder), /shape-eval and the eval\n    itself may name the evals folder.\n  impact_if_unknown: 'Garura has no build play for an epic yet (that work is business\n    intent #819). If the check names only some plays, a play that builds code but\n    is not on the list can be handed the eval, and a pass then proves less than the\n    intent asks.'\n  user_decision: accepted\n  user_answer: yes \u2014 accepted as proposed\n  resolved_at: '2026-10-26T06:52:29Z'\n  resolved_by_run: shape-slice-798-898", "version": null, "around": {"start": 4, "end": 36, "text": "\n```yaml\nquestions:\n- id: Q-builders-1\n  kind: asked\n  blocking: false\n  asked_at: '2026-10-26T06:32:34Z'\n  topic: builders\n  question: Which plays must the new check treat as build plays, whose inputs may\n    never name the evals folder?\n  proposed_answer: Every play, skill and agent that builds the software, and every\n    context sub-agent it starts, is a build play for the check. Only /shape-slice\n    (which writes the hidden file into the evals folder), /shape-eval and the eval\n    itself may name the evals folder.\n  basis:\n    kind: model\n    ref: product/product-os/software-delivery-planning/shape-eval/capability.md:4\n  pipeline_source: /shape-slice shape-slice-798-898\n  pipeline_guess: Every play, skill and agent that builds the software, and every\n    context sub-agent it starts, is a build play for the check. Only /shape-slice\n    (which writes the hidden file into the evals folder), /shape-eval and the eval\n    itself may name the evals folder.\n  impact_if_unknown: 'Garura has no build play for an epic yet (that work is business\n    intent #819). If the check names only some plays, a play that builds code but\n    is not on the list can be handed the eval, and a pass then proves less than the\n    intent asks.'\n  user_decision: accepted\n  user_answer: yes \u2014 accepted as proposed\n  resolved_at: '2026-10-26T06:52:29Z'\n  resolved_by_run: shape-slice-798-898\n- id: Q-flag-1\n  kind: asked\n  blocking: false"}}}], "from_update": null}, {"citation_id": "cite-20261026-025", "issue": 798, "play": "shape-slice", "question": "In which order are the features built?", "answer": "fn-795, then fn-818, then fn-798, then fn-898.", "decided_by": "author-slice (via product-os-keeper)", "decided_at": "2026-10-26T07:10:10Z", "trace": [{"asked": "what /shape-plan needs before it runs", "found": "/shape-plan runs after /shape-slice and reads the slice that serves the intent", "source": {"tier": "garura", "path": "product/product-os/software-delivery-planning/cap-718/fn-818/feature.md", "start": 4, "end": 4, "fingerprint": "sha256:994885950cc86d2453e28af308067e90cd83ed82d1ef9626e2a157812c7b8819", "text": "/shape-plan <intent> runs after /shape-slice, on its own. It reads the slice that serves the intent and the ICE of each feature and its capability, once. It writes the intent's one plan file, one epic for the slice, and one story for each feature. It never writes a failure or recovery condition: the slice's hidden file is /shape-slice's (decision 6 of #844). Not built yet (#818).", "version": null, "around": {"start": 1, "end": 7, "text": "# Feature: /shape-plan writes the plan, the epic and the stories\n\n## What it does\n/shape-plan <intent> runs after /shape-slice, on its own. It reads the slice that serves the intent and the ICE of each feature and its capability, once. It writes the intent's one plan file, one epic for the slice, and one story for each feature. It never writes a failure or recovery condition: the slice's hidden file is /shape-slice's (decision 6 of #844). Not built yet (#818).\n\n> To be deepened later: written by /shape-slice for bi-788 at the directional depth. /discover-domains or /discover-capabilities raises it to the detailed depth.\n"}}}, {"asked": "what /shape-eval needs before it runs", "found": "/shape-eval runs after /shape-plan and reads the epic, its stories and the slice's hidden file", "source": {"tier": "garura", "path": "product/product-os/software-delivery-planning/shape-eval/fn-798/feature.md", "start": 4, "end": 4, "fingerprint": "sha256:040588fb1725bd4ef117100580e5eac7418407a4c3f641d07e9f729fa24aa5ac", "text": "/shape-eval <intent> runs after /shape-plan, on its own. It reads the epic, its stories and the slice's hidden file, and writes the eval for the business intent in the plan's evals folder (.garura/project/plans/<plan-id>/evals/<slug>/). No build is given that folder: the build is given the business intent, never the eval (fn-898). Not built yet (#798).", "version": null, "around": {"start": 1, "end": 7, "text": "# Feature: /shape-eval writes the hidden eval\n\n## What it does\n/shape-eval <intent> runs after /shape-plan, on its own. It reads the epic, its stories and the slice's hidden file, and writes the eval for the business intent in the plan's evals folder (.garura/project/plans/<plan-id>/evals/<slug>/). No build is given that folder: the build is given the business intent, never the eval (fn-898). Not built yet (#798).\n\n> To be deepened later: written by /shape-slice for bi-788 at the directional depth. /discover-domains or /discover-capabilities raises it to the detailed depth.\n"}}}, {"asked": "when the checks of #898 are built", "found": "the design orders #898's checks (step 3) after /shape-eval (step 2)", "source": {"tier": "short-term", "path": "798/specs/design.md", "start": 22, "end": 23, "fingerprint": "sha256:f52dce5529cadbb199f4da8c79ecddf7a323312035ac9952c07deb5868d4e36a", "text": "3. #898: a lint check that no build play's inputs name the evals folder, the eval or the hidden file; a check over a build\n   session's ledger that flags a read of the evals folder (it flags, it does not block), with tests.", "version": null, "around": {"start": 19, "end": 26, "text": "2. `/shape-eval` (#798, through `/create-play`): reads the epic, its stories and the hidden file only; writes one eval\n   per slice into `plans/<plan>/evals/<slice>/`, in plain text; each check tests, from the outside through the usage\n   guide, what the business intent promises; anything it cannot test yet is named; one pinned checkpoint.\n3. #898: a lint check that no build play's inputs name the evals folder, the eval or the hidden file; a check over a build\n   session's ledger that flags a read of the evals folder (it flags, it does not block), with tests.\n4. The rules: ADR 049 (\"Encrypting the evals is #828\") and `docs/philosophy/idd-principles.md` (\"the evals are encrypted\")\n   say instead that the build is given the intent, never the eval (through `/record-decision`, amending ADR 049);\n   the ontology and `managing-work.md` match."}}}], "from_update": null}, {"citation_id": "cite-20261026-026", "issue": 798, "play": "shape-slice", "question": "Which surface does the tester use?", "answer": "the Claude Code command line", "decided_by": "author-slice (via product-os-keeper)", "decided_at": "2026-10-26T07:10:10Z", "trace": [{"asked": "the surface of the slice, as written", "found": "surf-claude-code-cli, the Claude Code command line, where the product owner runs /shape-slice, /shape-plan and /shape-eval", "source": {"tier": "garura", "path": "product/product-os/slices/sl-intent-to-design.yaml", "start": 16, "end": 21, "fingerprint": "sha256:4a2bf683f15724c3a5fd145970358fdd638197e1df4e8c2c04441040277a4130", "text": "surface:\n  id: surf-claude-code-cli\n  name: the Claude Code command line\n  persona_ref: product-owner\n  user_action: runs /shape-slice, then /shape-plan, then /shape-eval on a business\n    intent", "version": null, "around": {"start": 13, "end": 21, "text": "  vertical: the Claude Code command line\n  intents:\n  - bi-788\nsurface:\n  id: surf-claude-code-cli\n  name: the Claude Code command line\n  persona_ref: product-owner\n  user_action: runs /shape-slice, then /shape-plan, then /shape-eval on a business\n    intent"}}}, {"asked": "what the intent's outcome asks the product owner to do", "found": "the product owner names a piece of work and confirms each part as agents make it", "source": {"tier": "garura", "path": "product/product-os/intents/bi-788.md", "start": 3, "end": 3, "fingerprint": "sha256:2b57e7172fd80751ff52a570a3403dd241d0428ad66919276ada03cc1b2819ab", "text": "**Outcome:** The product owner names a piece of work. Agents shape it into a slice that one person can test, make its plan and write its eval. The product owner confirms each part as it is made.", "version": null, "around": {"start": 1, "end": 6, "text": "# Agents design a named piece of work\n\n**Outcome:** The product owner names a piece of work. Agents shape it into a slice that one person can test, make its plan and write its eval. The product owner confirms each part as it is made.\n\n**Why:** Today the product owner must guide each step of the design by hand. No play designs the work for Garura's own work: the product owner found this while #760 started. When agents do the design, the work is faster and it stays inside its design.\n"}}}], "from_update": null}, {"citation_id": "cite-20261026-027", "issue": 798, "play": "shape-slice", "question": "Who tests the slice?", "answer": "the product owner (persona product-owner)", "decided_by": "author-slice (via product-os-keeper)", "decided_at": "2026-10-26T07:10:10Z", "trace": [{"asked": "who asked for the intent", "found": "the product owner", "source": {"tier": "garura", "path": "product/product-os/intents/bi-788.md", "start": 7, "end": 7, "fingerprint": "sha256:de0d088eb3f5a54585f8dad0c95013110386f9f7a1d62b20f80df4d6a142a20b", "text": "**Asked by:** the product owner", "version": null, "around": {"start": 4, "end": 10, "text": "\n**Why:** Today the product owner must guide each step of the design by hand. No play designs the work for Garura's own work: the product owner found this while #760 started. When agents do the design, the work is faster and it stays inside its design.\n\n**Asked by:** the product owner\n\n**Proof it is met:**\n- A business intent goes from its issue to an approved design."}}}, {"asked": "the persona of the slice's surface, as written", "found": "persona_ref product-owner", "source": {"tier": "garura", "path": "product/product-os/slices/sl-intent-to-design.yaml", "start": 19, "end": 19, "fingerprint": "sha256:3d969030c31daee3dcfff40b9e7df245f6f7fbbfa1285f1acf0886cf77238ddf", "text": "  persona_ref: product-owner", "version": null, "around": {"start": 16, "end": 21, "text": "surface:\n  id: surf-claude-code-cli\n  name: the Claude Code command line\n  persona_ref: product-owner\n  user_action: runs /shape-slice, then /shape-plan, then /shape-eval on a business\n    intent"}}}], "from_update": null}, {"citation_id": "cite-20261026-028", "issue": 798, "play": "shape-slice", "question": "Which slice serves this business intent, and does it change?", "answer": "The kept slice sl-intent-to-design serves bi-788; it pulls in fn-898 and pushes out nothing.", "decided_by": "author-slice (via product-os-keeper)", "decided_at": "2026-10-26T07:10:10Z", "trace": [{"asked": "the rule that picks the kept slice", "found": "the slice sl-intent-to-design already lists business intent bi-788", "source": {"tier": "short-term", "path": "798/context/shape-slice/serving.json", "start": 2, "end": 3, "fingerprint": "sha256:800e4495dcc64c6accb19ab682d6ef8f14aa8ce92ab8138651f606b2a024444a", "text": "  \"match\": \"sl-intent-to-design\",\n  \"reason\": \"slice 'sl-intent-to-design' already lists business intent 'bi-788'\",", "version": null, "around": {"start": 1, "end": 6, "text": "{\n  \"match\": \"sl-intent-to-design\",\n  \"reason\": \"slice 'sl-intent-to-design' already lists business intent 'bi-788'\",\n  \"reuse_args\": [\n    \"--reuse\",\n    \"sl-intent-to-design\""}}}, {"asked": "whether a slice is in progress", "found": "no slice is in progress, so the kept slice may change", "source": {"tier": "short-term", "path": "798/context/shape-slice/serving.json", "start": 8, "end": 8, "fingerprint": "sha2